#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cepa-plan — writes, validates and reads the single-track queue.

It exists because step 1 of the "one writer, three sources" design (BACKLOG.md,
"Cinco portas de planejamento", approved on 2026-08-24) cannot live only in the
prose of a command: a `.md` that says "validate the `why` fields before writing"
erodes silently, and the damage only shows up when someone opens the plan months
later and the order has no recorded criterion at all. Here the refusal is code,
and a test exercises it.

Caller: `/common:queue`. The command holds the conversation (reads the spec, asks
for the order, pulls the `why` from wherever it is already written) and hands the
finished list to this script, which validates, resolves the right root, refuses
collisions and writes.

It only knows `mode: single-track`. Waves are another document, with another
author (`/maestro:program-plan`) and another consumer (`/maestro:run`).

Subcommands:

  cepa-plan migrate [<nome> | --all] [--dry-run] [--repo DIR]
      Moves the queue from the old layout (.claude/programs/<n>/plan.yaml, key
      `program:`) to .claude/queues/<n>/queue.yaml (key `queue:`), with the whole
      directory (until/ included) and one commit. Refuses: a LIVE session
      reservation, a destination that already exists. A wave plan is skipped.

  cepa-plan check-name <nome> [--repo DIR]
      Is the program name free for a QUEUE? Mirror of
      `maestro-programs --check-name`, which asks the same question from the
      other side.
      Exit 0 = free (or already a queue, and rewriting is the normal replanning
      flow); 3 = collision with a WAVES plan — writing the queue there erases
      the waves without a word.

  cepa-plan from-spec <docs/spec/slug.md> [--json]
      Reads a /common:spec specification and returns the list of items (JSON),
      one per success criterion `### CS-N`, IN TEXT ORDER. Writes nothing —
      the writer is `write`, which also accepts `--from-spec` directly.
      Each item's `why` is assembled from what the spec already wrote (Superfície
      e Teste vermelho) and, when the text does not say why that criterion comes
      before the others, it carries the sentence that records the inheritance
      instead of an invented criterion. Exit 2 = the spec has no criterion.

  cepa-plan from-triage <repasse.json|-> [--json]
      Reads the handoff of a /board-flow:triage triage — the classification of
      the cards into buckets, already in the execution order the owner
      confirmed — and returns the list of items (JSON). Writes nothing; the
      writer is `write`, which also accepts `--from-triage` directly.
      Only a `ready` card becomes a `pending` item: `implemented` belongs to
      the PROOF queue and `needs-refinement` stays in the backlog. `obsolete`
      enters as `dropped`, with the reason, so the discard does not vanish from
      the document. Refuses a READY card without `why`, an OBSOLETE card without
      a reason, and a card still parked in `needs-decision` (unfinished grid).
      Exit 2 = refused, with the reason.

  cepa-plan promote <nome> [--repo DIR] [--json] [--when AAAA-MM-DD]
      The demands the queue hands to `/maestro:program-plan --from-plan` —
      the queue → waves promotion, which until now was manual for lack of a
      path. Writes nothing, decides neither surface nor acceptance (that is the
      program-plan conversation) and does not touch the queue. Says three
      things only the queue knows: which items can become a slice, which
      CANNOT and why, and what wave floor `blocked_by` imposes on each one — an
      item that depends on another in the same promotion cannot fork in the
      same wave as it.
      Only `pending` becomes a demand: `in_progress` is reserved by another
      session (forking on top duplicates the work), `blocked` left a previous
      run stuck on an outside condition nobody touched, and `done`/`dropped`
      already left the queue. An open `human_pending` does not vanish: it
      becomes `human_gate: "open: <rota>"` in the slice, which is what cepa-dor
      fails until someone decides. Exit 3 = the plan is a waves plan (nothing
      to promote); 4 = D7 floor (< 4 demands) — below it the fork loses to
      /common:drain-plan, which executes the same queue with no worktree at all.

  cepa-plan queue <nome> [--max N] [--repo DIR] [--json]
      The items `/common:drain-plan` can execute NOW, in queue order, and the
      reason the batch stops where it stops. It does not execute and writes
      nothing. Walks the list from the start and stops at the first thing it
      cannot resolve by itself — an open `human_pending`, an item blocked by
      something that is not in the batch, an item already reserved by another
      session, or the cap. Skipping a stuck item to reach the one below would be
      reordering the queue silently, which is what this document exists to
      prevent.

  cepa-plan ready [--repo DIR] [--json]
      The items ready to be built NOW, across EVERY single-track queue of the
      repo, each queue in its recorded order. Reads only. "Ready" is what
      `build_batch` would hand a run with no ceiling: `pending` with no open
      `human_pending`, no unresolved `blocked_by`, not reserved by a live
      session. `status` answers this for one queue and refuses to pick when
      there are several; this is the view of the whole repo (owner,
      2026-11-05: "os itens prontos para serem construídos de todas as filas
      disponíveis"). A queue with nothing ready is still listed, in one line,
      with what holds it. An unreadable queue is warned and skipped.
      Exit 0 = shown (even with zero ready, even when every queue file is
      unreadable — there IS a queue, it is sick); 2 = no queue file at all.

  cepa-plan reconcile <nome> --board ARQUIVO [--apply] [--repo DIR] [--json]
      The queue against the board: who closed outside the plan, who vanished,
      and which cards exist on the board with no position in the queue. It used
      to be the prose table in /common:next; it became code so the batch can
      reconcile without rewriting the rule — and so the rule has a test.
      Does not talk to Jira: the one who reads the board is `atlassian-expert`,
      and its result arrives here through `--board`. `--apply` writes; without
      it, reports. NEVER closes a `human_pending` (only the human closes it)
      and NEVER appends a card the queue does not have (a position without
      `why` is the decision the queue keeps — whoever places it is
      /common:queue --from-jira). And NEVER demotes a `done` item (rule R3): a
      card that went backwards on the board becomes a warning.

  cepa-plan start <nome> <id>
      Reserves the item: `pending` → `in_progress`, and SIGNS the reservation
      with the owning session (`claimed_by`: session_id, pid, hostname, cwd,
      time). It is the reservation that keeps two sessions from building the
      same item — the tracker-less equivalent of the claim /board-flow:drain
      publishes on the card. With a live owner, the refusal NAMES who is on the
      item; with a dead owner, the reservation is orphaned and claiming it is
      right, otherwise the queue jams forever because of a run that ended.
      Liveness is `_wtlib`'s (pid alive on the same host, 24h horizon), the
      same as the worktree system — two copies of the rule diverge.

  cepa-plan finish <nome> <id> --status done|blocked|pending --evidence TEXTO
                   [--human-pending ROTA]
      Records the outcome. `--evidence` is mandatory: `done` without what
      happened is just a word, and this repo's queue keeps the evidence of each
      closed item. `--human-pending` OPENS a route only the human closes;
      closing it (passing empty) is refused, because only whoever ran the route
      knows whether it passed.
      `--status done` is refused when the `.claude/last-build.json` at the
      root of the `--repo` session is EMPTY (a test filter that matched zero
      tests): green without a test does not close an item.
      It is also refused when the session topology (`.claude/topology`) has
      `validation-lead` (build-hex, build-team) and there is no
      `docs/validation/<id>.yaml` (or the legacy `.claude/validation/<id>.yaml`)
      with `verdict: READY-TO-SHIP` or
      `READY-WITH-CAVEATS`: without it the item closes without the security
      review.

  cepa-plan add <nome> <id> --title T [--why W] [--before <id>]
                [--blocked-by id1,id2] [--repo DIR]
      A1 of "Fila única" (BACKLOG.md): appends ONE item to a queue that already
      exists, without rewriting the others — unlike `write`, which replaces the
      whole list. It is what `/board-flow:capture`, `cepa-feedback triage` (when
      the destination is cepa) and the owner's own hand call so a new card does
      not stay only in Jira or only in BACKLOG.md.
      Without `--before`, the item enters at the END of the queue and the `why`
      carries the phrase "ainda não priorizado" (rule R2: every entry door
      creates the item in the same step, even without knowing the position).
      With `--before`, `--why` is MANDATORY — a position chosen without the
      reason it comes before the others is exactly what the queue exists to
      prevent.
      Exit 2 = missing queue, `--before` or `--blocked-by` pointing to an id
      that is not in this queue, or the result does not pass
      `validate_plan`; 3 = waves plan; 4 = id already exists (the message
      states its status, so a caller that calls twice can tell).

  cepa-plan order <nome> --keys K1,K2,... [--json] [--repo DIR]
      A2: gives `/board-flow:drain` the queue order for a list of Jira keys.
      The ones that are plan items come first, in queue order; the ones that
      are not come after, in the order they arrived (Jira's), marked
      `fora_do_plano`. Does not decide what to do with a `done`/`dropped` item —
      only orders and states the status of each key beside it. Exit 2 = missing
      queue (the caller falls back to the Jira order).

  cepa-plan divergence <nome> [--board ARQUIVO] [--backlog ARQUIVO]
                        [--json] [--repo DIR]
      A3: what `/common:doctor` lists without fixing anything — read-only, on
      purpose, because deciding on its own (closing an orphan card, inventing a
      `**Plano:**`) is rewriting the queue or the document without the owner
      seeing. Three lists: `cards_sem_item` (card open in Jira with no item in
      the plan), `itens_com_card_done` (unclosed item whose card the board
      already says is `done`) and `secoes_sem_plano`/`plano_inexistente`
      (BACKLOG.md section without the `**Plano:**` line, or citing an id that is
      not in this queue). Without `--board`, the first two are left out of the
      report (warned, not silenced); without `--backlog`, the third too.
      Exit 0 even with divergence — it is a report, not a failure; 2 =
      any of the input files is unreadable.

  cepa-plan validate <name | plan.yaml> [--repo DIR]
      The checks below, on a queue already on disk: a queue NAME is resolved at
      the main clone (even from a linked worktree); an existing file path is
      validated as given (no git needed, so `/tmp/queue.yaml` drafts work).
      Exit 0 = valid; 2 = invalid, with the gaps named.

  cepa-plan write <nome> --items ARQUIVO|- | --from-spec F | --from-triage F
                  [--source TEXTO] [--repo DIR]
                  [--on-missing refuse|keep|drop] [--dry-run]
      Writes the queue. Items come in as a JSON or YAML file (a list of
      objects) or through stdin with `-`.
      Exit 0 = written; 2 = invalid items; 3 = name collision; 4 = the file on
      disk has items the new list does not mention (see --on-missing).
      `--on-missing keep` puts those items at the end; with `--from-triage` it
      is the partial triage, and it is the opposite: the queue on disk keeps its
      order and the new cards enter after.
      With `--from-triage` there is no exit 4: the absent `done`/`dropped` are
      preserved (as a block, at the start), the triage items enter in its order
      and the absent open ones go after (warned); `--on-missing drop` marks
      only those open ones as `dropped`.

Item checks — each one exists because the corresponding failure already cost
someone something:

  - `id` present and UNIQUE. A repeated id makes `blocked_by` point to two
    items and /common:next pick one of them silently.
  - `title` present.
  - `why` present and non-empty. It is THE field of the document: the schema
    calls it "the field that evaporates today". A queue without `why` keeps the
    order and loses the criterion, and the first doubt ("does it still make
    sense?") forces reprioritizing from scratch — which is exactly the pain the
    plan exists to remove.
  - `status` in the closed vocabulary (pending|in_progress|done|blocked|dropped).
  - `blocked_by` points only to ids that exist in THIS queue. A phantom id
    leaves the item blocked forever by something nobody will close.
  - no cycle in `blocked_by`. Two items that block each other vanish from the
    /common:next answer with no warning: neither is a candidate, and the queue
    seems simply to have ended.
  - `human_pending` with the key PRESENT (the value may be null). An explicit
    null is an answer ("not applicable, internal substrate"); a missing key is
    an omission, and the debt to the human becomes invisible again, which is the
    reason for the field.
  - at least one item.

Rewrite (the name is already a queue): the new list rules ORDER, `title` and
`why` — which are planning decisions. What came from execution comes from disk:

  - The disk `status` always wins. Whoever executed knows where the item is;
    whoever replans is deciding order, not progress.
  - The disk `human_pending` wins while it is OPEN (non-null). Only the human
    closes that pending item, and the new list carries `null` on every item by
    default — taking it literally would erase the debt exactly when
    reprioritizing, which is when it most needs to show up. A null on disk
    accepts the new route the list brought.

What the rewrite does NOT preserve: hand-written comments in the file (this
repo's `cepa` plan has several, with the evidence of each `done`). Before
overwriting, the previous file is copied to `<arquivo>.bak` and the path comes
out in the report.
"""
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import subprocess
import sys
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "hooks"))
import _tui  # noqa: E402
import _clihelp  # noqa: E402

try:
    import yaml
except ImportError:
    print("cepa-plan precisa de PyYAML (pip install pyyaml)", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(2)

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "hooks"))
import _queuepath as qp  # noqa: E402  (resolver for both queue layouts)
import _ownertext  # noqa: E402  (the human section of a blocked item)
import _decisions  # noqa: E402  (the one reader of "Decided without asking")
import _state  # noqa: E402  (the one reader of the state deposits and the run liveness rule)
from _state import HEARTBEAT_STALE_SEC  # noqa: E402,F401  (one copy of the constant)

MODE = "single-track"
SCHEMA_VERSION = 2
STATUSES = ("pending", "in_progress", "done", "blocked", "dropped")
CLOSED = ("done", "dropped")
DEFAULT_MAX = 3


def status_of(it):
    return it.get("status", "pending")


def now_iso():
    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec="seconds")


# ── who holds the item: the reservation has an owner, and the owner has liveness ──
#
# Until 2026-08-28 `start` wrote only `status: in_progress`, and nothing else.
# With that, the question "is another session on it right now, or did a run die
# and leave the status behind?" was UNDECIDABLE from the file — `queue` could
# only offer both readings and stop the batch. The session registry the worktree
# system already keeps (`.claude/sessions/<key>.json`, with `pid`, `hostname` and
# `last_seen`) answers exactly that question, and `_wtlib.entry_is_live` already
# implements the rule: PID alive on the same host, and nothing beyond the 24h
# horizon (`_wtlib.STALE_HOURS`). Reserving here means writing an entry in that
# same format, so liveness is the SAME function — two copies of the rule
# diverge, and this repo has already paid for that.

def _wt():
    """`_wtlib`, imported from the sibling `common/hooks/`. None if unavailable."""
    global _WTLIB
    try:
        return _WTLIB
    except NameError:
        pass
    path = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "hooks"
    if str(path) not in sys.path:
        sys.path.insert(0, str(path))
    try:
        import _wtlib as m
    except ImportError:
        m = None
    _WTLIB = m
    return m


def current_owner(root, cwd):
    """The session entry that will sign the reservation.

    Prefers the LIVE session registered for this tree: its pid is that of the
    `claude` process, which is what keeps existing after this script dies.
    With no registry (harness not installed, ad-hoc call), falls back to the
    calling process — worse, but named, and better than signing with a pid
    that dies in the same second.
    """
    w = _wt()
    if w:
        live = w.live_sessions_in(str(root), str(cwd))
        # DUR-2 hardening: a second live session may register in the same tree
        # between `start` and `finish` (the owner's interactive one). Taking the
        # first entry would refuse the agent on its own item, so the session the
        # caller says it is (CLAUDE_SESSION_ID) wins when it is registered.
        mine = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_SESSION_ID")
        live.sort(key=lambda e: e.get("session_id") != mine)
        for e in live[:1]:
            return {"session_id": e.get("session_id"), "pid": e.get("pid"),
                    "hostname": e.get("hostname") or w.host(),
                    "cwd": e.get("cwd") or str(cwd), "branch": e.get("branch"),
                    "started_at": now_iso()}
    return {"session_id": os.environ.get("CLAUDE_SESSION_ID")
            or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_WT_CLAIM") or "sessão não registrada",
            "pid": os.getppid(), "hostname": w.host() if w else "?",
            "cwd": str(cwd), "branch": None, "started_at": now_iso()}


# A reservation held from ANOTHER host is live only while the run that holds it keeps
# writing its heartbeat; the rule (and HEARTBEAT_STALE_SEC) lives in `_state.run_liveness`.


def run_heartbeat_of(root, claimed_by):
    """The newest run state (`*.estado.json` under `.claude/queues/*/until/` or
    `.claude/programs/*/until/`) whose `host` and `arvore` are the reservation's
    `hostname` and `cwd` AND that carries a `heartbeat`. (path, state) or None."""
    if not root:
        return None
    best = None
    for layout in ("queues", "programs"):
        for path in Path(root).glob(f".claude/{layout}/*/until/*.estado.json"):
            try:
                est = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                continue
            if not isinstance(est, dict) or not est.get("heartbeat"):
                continue
            if est.get("host") != claimed_by.get("hostname") \
                    or est.get("arvore") != claimed_by.get("cwd"):
                continue
            if best is None or str(est["heartbeat"]) > str(best[1]["heartbeat"]):
                best = (path, est)
    return best


def reservation_of(it, root=None):
    """(state, detail) of an `in_progress` item.

      - `viva`     — has an owner and the owner responds. Executing on top
                     would duplicate the work of whoever is on it right now.
      - `orfa`     — has an owner and the owner no longer exists (dead pid on
                     the same host, or entry beyond the 24h horizon; a pid on
                     another machine cannot be probed, so there only age counts).
                     The reservation is recoverable.
      - `sem-dono` — `in_progress` without `claimed_by`: queue marked before
                     this registry existed, or written by hand. Undecidable, and
                     the honest thing is to say so instead of guessing one of
                     the two.

    A reservation from another host can't be pid-probed. When `root` is given and a
    run state file of that host/worktree carries a `heartbeat`, its age decides
    (HEARTBEAT_STALE_SEC, and the run must still say `rodando`); with no such file,
    the 24h rule stands.
    """
    c = it.get("claimed_by")
    if not isinstance(c, dict) or not c:
        return "sem-dono", (
            "reservado sem dono registrado — a marcação é anterior ao registro "
            "de dono, ou foi escrita à mão. Não dá para dizer se é sessão viva "
            "ou run morto; devolver para `pending` é decisão sua "
            "(`cepa-plan finish <fila> <id> --status pending --evidence ...`)")
    who = c.get("session_id") or "?"
    where = c.get("cwd") or "?"
    since = c.get("started_at") or "?"
    w = _wt()
    is_live = w.entry_is_live(c) if w else True
    if w and root and c.get("hostname") not in (None, w.host()):
        found = run_heartbeat_of(root, c)
        if found:
            path, est = found
            live_state, _ = _state.run_liveness(est)
            age = _state.heartbeat_age(est)
            if live_state == "vivo":
                return "viva", (f"sessão {who} está nele desde {since} "
                                f"(host {c.get('hostname')}, {where}); o run "
                                f"{path.name} bateu o coração há {int(age)}s")
            if live_state != "desconhecido" and age is not None:
                # `desconhecido` (no readable heartbeat, or one in the future) falls
                # through to the 24h rule: "cannot tell" never recovers a reservation.
                return "orfa", (f"a sessão {who} que reservou em {since} não existe "
                                f"mais: o run {path.name} (host {c.get('hostname')}) "
                                f"está `{est.get('estado')}` e o último heartbeat "
                                f"tem {int(age)}s")
    if is_live:
        return "viva", (f"sessão {who} está nele desde {since} "
                        f"(host {c.get('hostname')}, pid {c.get('pid')}, {where})")
    return "orfa", (f"a sessão {who} que reservou em {since} não existe mais "
                    f"(host {c.get('hostname')}, pid {c.get('pid')})")


def main_root(repo):
    """The main clone, even when called from inside a linked worktree.

    Same resolution as /common:next, /maestro:run and maestro-programs: the
    parent of `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` without the trailing `/.git`.
    Writing against the current directory is the "layer 0" defect — in a repo
    whose .gitignore covers `.claude/`, the plan becomes invisible to git and
    dies with the worktree.
    """
    r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(repo), "rev-parse", "--git-common-dir"],
                       capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        return None
    p = Path(r.stdout.strip())
    if not p.is_absolute():
        p = (Path(repo) / p).resolve()
    return p.parent if p.name == ".git" else p


def queue_path(root, name):
    """The `name` queue in both layouts (new one wins; absent → new path)."""
    return qp.queue_file(root, name)


def read_plan(path):
    """Returns (plan, error). An unreadable file does not blow up: it becomes a named error."""
    try:
        return (yaml.safe_load(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")) or {}), None
    except (yaml.YAMLError, OSError) as e:
        return None, f"{path} está ilegível ({e.__class__.__name__}: {e})"


def mode_of(plan):
    """v1 had no `mode`; absent there means waves (common/plan-schema.yaml)."""
    return plan.get("mode") or (
        "parallel-waves" if plan.get("schema_version") == 1 else None)


# ── validation ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def validate_items(items):
    """List of gaps in pt-BR. Empty = valid."""
    gaps = []
    if not isinstance(items, list) or not items:
        return ["a fila não tem nenhum item — um plano vazio não responde "
                "'o que eu faço agora?'"]

    seen = {}
    for i, it in enumerate(items, 1):
        where = f"item {i}"
        if not isinstance(it, dict):
            gaps.append(f"{where}: não é um objeto com campos, e sim {type(it).__name__}")
            continue
        ident = it.get("id")
        where = f"item {i} ({ident})" if ident else where
        if not ident or not str(ident).strip():
            gaps.append(f"{where}: sem `id` — o /common:next não tem como "
                          "nomear o passo nem o `blocked_by` como apontar")
        elif str(ident) in seen:
            gaps.append(f"{where}: `id` repetido (já usado no item "
                          f"{seen[str(ident)]}) — `blocked_by` passa a apontar "
                          "para dois itens e a escolha vira silenciosa")
        else:
            seen[str(ident)] = i

        if not str(it.get("title") or "").strip():
            gaps.append(f"{where}: sem `title`")
        if not str(it.get("why") or "").strip():
            gaps.append(f"{where}: sem `why` — a fila guardaria a ordem e "
                          "perderia o critério dela, que é o ponto do documento")

        st = it.get("status", "pending")
        if st not in STATUSES:
            gaps.append(f"{where}: `status` '{st}' fora do vocabulário "
                          f"{'|'.join(STATUSES)}")

        bb = it.get("blocked_by", [])
        if not isinstance(bb, list):
            gaps.append(f"{where}: `blocked_by` tem que ser lista (veio "
                          f"{type(bb).__name__})")
        elif ident and str(ident) in [str(x) for x in bb]:
            gaps.append(f"{where}: `blocked_by` aponta para o próprio item")

        if "human_pending" not in it:
            gaps.append(f"{where}: sem a chave `human_pending` — nulo explícito "
                          "é resposta válida ('não aplicável (substrato interno)'), "
                          "a chave ausente é omissão, e a dívida com o humano "
                          "volta a ser invisível")

    # phantom references and cycles only make sense with the ids already collected
    ids = set(seen)
    graph = {}
    for it in items:
        if not isinstance(it, dict):
            continue
        ident = str(it.get("id") or "")
        bb = it.get("blocked_by", [])
        if not isinstance(bb, list):
            continue
        targets = [str(x) for x in bb]
        for target in targets:
            if target not in ids:
                gaps.append(f"item {ident}: `blocked_by` cita '{target}', que não "
                              "existe nesta fila — o item ficaria bloqueado para "
                              "sempre por algo que ninguém vai fechar")
        graph[ident] = [a for a in targets if a in ids]

    for cycle in find_cycles(graph):
        gaps.append("ciclo em `blocked_by`: " + " → ".join(cycle) +
                      " — nenhum deles vira candidato, e a fila parece ter "
                      "acabado em vez de estar travada")
    return gaps


def find_cycles(graph):
    """Cycles of the blocking graph, each as a list of ids closing the loop."""
    cycles, state, stack = [], {}, []

    def visit(n):
        state[n] = "abrindo"
        stack.append(n)
        for m in graph.get(n, []):
            if state.get(m) == "abrindo":
                cycles.append(stack[stack.index(m):] + [m])
            elif m not in state:
                visit(m)
        stack.pop()
        state[n] = "fechado"

    for n in graph:
        if n not in state:
            visit(n)
    return cycles


def validate_plan(plan):
    """Gaps of a whole plan (header + items)."""
    gaps = []
    if plan.get("schema_version") not in (1, 2):
        gaps.append(f"`schema_version` é {plan.get('schema_version')!r}; "
                      "esperado 2")
    if mode_of(plan) != MODE:
        # Stops HERE on purpose: continuing to list queue gaps on a document
        # that is not a queue sends the owner to fix the wrong thing — they
        # would read "the queue has no items" about a perfectly valid waves plan
        # and go tamper with it.
        return [f"`mode` é {mode_of(plan)!r}, não '{MODE}' — este script só "
                "escreve e valida fila; ondas são do /maestro:program-plan, e "
                "quem as executa é o /maestro:run"]
    if plan.get("schema_version") == 1 and plan.get("mode") == MODE:
        gaps.append("um plano v1 não pode declarar 'single-track': o modo não "
                      "existia lá. Suba `schema_version` para 2")
    if not str(qp.queue_name_of(plan, "")).strip():
        gaps.append("sem `queue` (nem `program`, a chave do layout antigo)")
    if not str(plan.get("source") or "").strip():
        gaps.append("sem `source` — de onde as demandas vieram é o que permite "
                      "conferir a fila contra a fonte depois")
    demo_key = _demonstrates_key(plan)
    if demo_key:
        d = plan.get(demo_key)
        if not isinstance(d, str) or not d.strip():
            gaps.append(f"`{demo_key}` é {d!r} — o campo é opcional, mas se "
                          "estiver no cabeçalho tem que ser uma frase dizendo "
                          "o que a fila demonstra quando acaba")
    gaps.extend(validate_items(plan.get("items")))
    return gaps


# ── writing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

HEADER = """\
# {arquivo} — fila `single-track`, escrita por /common:queue.
#
# ORDEM DA LISTA = ordem de execução; é o dado. O `why` de cada item é o
# critério que colocou ele nessa posição — sem ele a fila guarda a ordem e
# perde o motivo. Schema anotado: common/plan-schema.yaml.
#
# Quem lê: /common:next (nomeia UM próximo passo). `human_pending` só o humano
# fecha — agente nenhum troca o texto por null por conta própria.
#
# Fonte das demandas: {fonte}
# Escrito em: {quando}
"""


SCHEMA_KEYS = ("id", "title", "why", "status", "blocked_by", "human_pending")


def normalize(it):
    """Item with the schema keys first, and the rest PRESERVED at the end.

    Silently discarding a key someone wrote by hand is this house's failure:
    the field vanishes on the first reprioritization and nobody notices,
    because the file stays valid. An unknown key is not an error — it is
    someone recording something the schema has not foreseen yet (the evidence
    of a `done`, for example).
    """
    base = {
        "id": it["id"],
        "title": it["title"],
        "why": it["why"],
        "status": it.get("status", "pending"),
        "blocked_by": [str(x) for x in it.get("blocked_by", [])],
        "human_pending": it.get("human_pending", None),
    }
    for k, v in it.items():
        if k not in SCHEMA_KEYS:
            base[k] = v
    return base


def merge(new_items, old_items):
    """The new list rules order/title/why; the disk rules what is execution.

    Preserving `status` and `human_pending` is not a convenience: only the
    human closes a `human_pending`, so a rewrite that zeroed them would erase
    debt nobody paid — and the debt would vanish from the only place that
    showed it.
    """
    by_id = {str(a.get("id")): a for a in (old_items or []) if isinstance(a, dict)}
    output, reused = [], []
    for it in new_items:
        base = normalize(it)
        old = by_id.get(str(it["id"]))
        if old:
            # Progress is a word of EXECUTION; abandonment is a word of
            # PLANNING. So the disk `status` wins — except when the new list
            # says `dropped`, which is someone deciding the item no longer
            # belongs to the queue. Without this exception the writer cannot
            # retire any item, and the queue only grows (found on the 1st real
            # use: an item that step 1 itself made obsolete came back `pending`).
            # What it still cannot do is claim progress the disk does not have:
            # a `done` coming from the new list is ignored.
            if old.get("status") and it.get("status") != "dropped":
                base["status"] = old["status"]
            # The disk `human_pending` wins while it is OPEN. Only the human
            # closes that pending item — and the new list carries `null` on
            # every item by default, so taking it literally would erase the debt
            # exactly when reprioritizing. A null on disk accepts the new route.
            if old.get("human_pending") is not None:
                base["human_pending"] = old["human_pending"]
            for k, v in old.items():
                if k not in SCHEMA_KEYS and k not in base:
                    base[k] = v
            reused.append(str(it["id"]))
        output.append(base)
    return output, reused


def _demonstrates_key(plan):
    """The key of the script that the file carries: `demonstrates`, or `demonstra`
    (queues written before the rename); None if it has neither."""
    for key in ("demonstrates", "demonstra"):
        if key in plan:
            return key
    return None


def _read_demonstrates(plan):
    key = _demonstrates_key(plan)
    return plan.get(key) if key else None


def serialize(name, source, items, when, demonstrates=None, key="queue"):
    body = {
        "schema_version": SCHEMA_VERSION,
        "mode": MODE,
        key: name,
        "source": source,
    }
    # `demonstrates` only exists when someone wrote it: a queue without it stays
    # valid, and a `demonstrates: null` written by default would be noise.
    if demonstrates:
        body["demonstrates"] = demonstrates
    body["items"] = items
    dump = yaml.dump(body, allow_unicode=True, sort_keys=False,
                     default_flow_style=False, width=78)
    filename = qp.NEW_FILE if key == "queue" else qp.LEGACY_FILE
    return HEADER.format(fonte=source, quando=when, arquivo=filename) + "\n" + dump


def load_items(origin):
    """JSON or YAML, from a file or from stdin ('-'). Returns (items, error)."""
    try:
        raw = sys.stdin.read() if origin == "-" else Path(origin).read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except OSError as e:
        return None, f"não deu para ler {origin}: {e}"
    if not raw.strip():
        return None, f"{origin} veio vazio"
    try:
        data = json.loads(raw)
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        try:
            data = yaml.safe_load(raw)
        except yaml.YAMLError as e:
            return None, f"{origin} não é JSON nem YAML válido ({e})"
    # accepts both the bare list and a document with `items:`
    if isinstance(data, dict) and "items" in data:
        data = data["items"]
    if not isinstance(data, list):
        return None, (f"{origin} tem que trazer uma LISTA de itens (ou um "
                      "documento com `items:`)")
    return data, None


# ── reading a /common:spec specification ─────────────────────────────────────

INHERITED = ("herdado da ordem do texto da especificação; ninguém priorizou os "
           "critérios entre si")

RE_CRITERION = re.compile(r"^###\s+(CS-\d+)\s*:\s*(.+?)\s*$", re.M)
# The field may span SEVERAL lines — a real "Teste vermelho" is usually a whole
# sentence broken across three lines. Capturing only the first produced a `why`
# cut in the middle of a clause, which is worse than not having the field: it
# looks like complete text. It runs until the next line that opens another
# field, a heading, or the blank line that closes the paragraph.
RE_FIELD = re.compile(
    r"^\*\*(Superfície|Surface|Teste vermelho|Red test)[:]?\*\*[:]?[ \t]*(.*?)"
    r"(?=\n[ \t]*\n|\n\*\*|\n#{2,}|\Z)", re.M | re.S)

# The English fields (Surface, Red test) and the old ones are both valid;
# `fields` always keeps the old name, which is the key of the `why` already
# written in the queues.
CANONICAL_FIELD = {"Surface": "Superfície", "Red test": "Teste vermelho"}

# The dependency the spec ITSELF declares in prose ("Depois do CS-1, ..."). It
# is the only one read from the text without deduction: two criteria touching
# the same file is not a dependency. The rule used to be "the agent appends
# wherever the spec declares", and on 2026-09-23 nobody appended — the queue
# released CS-2 before CS-1 existed.
RE_AFTER = re.compile(
    r"\b(?:depois|ap[óo]s)\s+(?:(?:d[oa]s?|[oa]s?)\s+)?"
    r"(CS-\d+(?:\s*(?:,|\be\b)\s*CS-\d+)*)", re.I)


def items_from_spec(text):
    """(items, warnings). One item per `### CS-N`, in the order they appear.

    The order is the text's, and the `why` SAYS so when the spec gave no reason
    for the position — the preference recorded in the design. Inventing here a
    priority nobody declared would be fabricating a decision, which is exactly
    what this document exists not to do.
    """
    warnings = []
    m = re.search(r"^\*\*Status:\*\*\s*(\S+)", text, re.M)
    status = m.group(1) if m else None
    if status not in ("ready-to-build", "pronta-para-construir"):
        warnings.append(f"a especificação está com `Status: {status}` — só "
                      "`ready-to-build` passou pelo crivo do /common:spec "
                      "(toda superfície observável e todo teste vermelho "
                      "declarados)")
    open_items = len(re.findall(r"^-\s+\[ \]", text, re.M))
    if open_items:
        warnings.append(f"{open_items} pergunta(s) ainda em aberto na spec — um "
                      "critério cuja pergunta não foi respondida vira item de "
                      "fila que ninguém sabe quando terminou")

    found = list(RE_CRITERION.finditer(text))
    ids = {m.group(1) for m in found}
    items = []
    for i, m in enumerate(found):
        body = text[m.end():found[i + 1].start() if i + 1 < len(found) else len(text)]
        depends = []
        for d in RE_AFTER.finditer(body):
            for target in re.findall(r"CS-\d+", d.group(1)):
                if target == m.group(1) or target in depends:
                    continue
                if target not in ids:
                    warnings.append(f"{m.group(1)} diz que vem depois do {target}, "
                                  "que não existe nesta spec — dependência "
                                  "fora do `blocked_by`")
                    continue
                depends.append(target)
        fields = {CANONICAL_FIELD.get(k, k): " ".join(v.split())
                  for k, v in RE_FIELD.findall(body)}
        pieces = [INHERITED]
        if fields.get("Superfície"):
            pieces.append(f"superfície onde se observa: {fields['Superfície']}")
        if fields.get("Teste vermelho"):
            pieces.append(f"teste vermelho declarado: {fields['Teste vermelho']}")
        else:
            warnings.append(f"{m.group(1)} não declara **Red test:** — o "
                          "item nasce sem a frase que diz quando ele terminou")
        items.append({
            "id": m.group(1),
            "title": m.group(2),
            "why": " · ".join(pieces),
            "status": "pending",
            "blocked_by": depends,
            "human_pending": None,
        })
    return items, warnings


def cmd_from_spec(path, as_json=True):
    p = Path(path)
    if not p.is_file():
        print(f"{p} não existe", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    items, warnings = items_from_spec(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    for a in warnings:
        print(f"aviso: {a}", file=sys.stderr)
    if not items:
        print(f"{p} não tem nenhum critério de sucesso (`### CS-N: ...`) — não "
              "há fila a escrever a partir dela", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    print(json.dumps(items, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) if as_json else items)
    return 0


# ── reading a cycle of an /common:epic Epic ──────────────────────────────────

INHERITED_EPIC = ("herdado da ordem do texto da coluna \"What it crosses\"; "
                "ninguém priorizou as peças entre si")

# The ladder columns the queue uses, by the start of the lowercase header — the
# same rule as the Epic check in spec-readiness-gate. "Efeito em tela" and
# "Efeito em backend" are optional HERE: the Epic written by hand before
# /common:epic (docs/epics/cepa-em-espiral.md) does not have them, and refusing
# it would leave the harness's first Epic without a queue.
# Each column is valid with the English name (new) and the old Portuguese one.
QUEUE_COLUMNS = ((("cycle", "ciclo"), "Cycle"),
                   (("script", "roteiro"), "Script"),
                   (("effect on screen", "efeito em tela"), "Effect on screen"),
                   (("effect in backend", "efeito em backend"),
                    "Effect in backend"),
                   (("what it crosses", "what crosses", "o que atravessa"),
                    "What it crosses"))
REQUIRED_COLUMNS = ("ciclo", "roteiro", "o que atravessa")  # canonical keys
# The key by which the rest of the function refers to each column (the old one).
CANONICAL_COLUMN = {c[0]: c[0][-1] for c in QUEUE_COLUMNS}
EMPTY_CELL = ("", "—", "–", "-", "nenhum", "nenhuma", "n/d", "nd")

RE_SECTION = re.compile(r"^##\s+(.+?)\s*$", re.M)

# What the Epic says beyond the pieces (2026-11-10, after the cycle-1 queue of
# wego-product `leitura-de-guias-fase-0-kairos.md` needed 16 items beyond its
# 15 pieces). Three rules that had no owner:
#   - `[espera: <condition>]` inside a piece is a precondition only a human
#     closes (a test by hand, a document). The item is born with it in
#     `human_pending`, so the batch defers it instead of building on a guess;
#   - a criterion the piece cites by id (`CA-9.4`) goes into the item's `why`
#     with its text, and a criterion no piece cites is a warning: the queue
#     reads only "What it crosses", so it would get no item;
#   - the last item of every cycle is the script itself, blocked by all the
#     pieces. The pieces are written per component; without this item nobody
#     owns the junction between them and the cycle "closes" piece by piece.
RE_WAIT = re.compile(r"\s*\[\s*espera\s*:\s*([^\]]*)\]", re.I)
RE_EPIC_CRITERION = re.compile(
    r"^\s*[-*+]\s+(?:\*\*|__)(CA-\d+(?:\.\d+)*[A-Za-z]?)(?:\*\*|__)\s*(.*)$",
    re.M)
RE_CRITERION_ID = re.compile(r"CA-\d+(?:\.\d+)*[A-Za-z]?")
OUT_OF_LADDER = "fora da escada"
SCRIPT_ITEM_TITLE = ("O roteiro do ciclo roda de ponta a ponta, com as peças "
                     "ligadas entre si")


def script_item_id(cycle):
    return f"C{cycle}-R"


def shorten(text, limit=240):
    text = " ".join(text.split())
    return text if len(text) <= limit else text[:limit - 1].rstrip() + "…"


def row_cells(line):
    """The cells of a table row. `\\|` is an escaped bar inside the
    cell, not a divider — the same rule as spec-readiness-gate."""
    s = line.strip()
    if s.startswith("|"):
        s = s[1:]
    if s.endswith("|") and not s.endswith("\\|"):
        s = s[:-1]
    return [c.strip().replace("\\|", "|") for c in re.split(r"(?<!\\)\|", s)]


def sentences_of(cell):
    """One sentence per piece: the text split at `.` or `;` followed by a space or
    the end, outside backticks. /common:epic writes the column in short
    sentences ending in a period; the Epic written by hand before it separates
    the pieces with `;`. It does not split inside backticks, otherwise
    `docs/epics/x.md` would become two, nor inside square brackets, where the
    `[espera: ...]` marker lives."""
    sentences, current, in_backtick, depth = [], [], False, 0
    for i, ch in enumerate(cell):
        if ch == "`":
            in_backtick = not in_backtick
        elif not in_backtick and ch == "[":
            depth += 1      # `[espera: ...]` may carry a period of its own
        elif not in_backtick and ch == "]" and depth:
            depth -= 1
        if (ch in ".;" and not in_backtick and not depth
                and (i + 1 == len(cell) or cell[i + 1].isspace())):
            sentences.append("".join(current))
            current = []
            continue
        current.append(ch)
    sentences.append("".join(current))
    return [" ".join(f.split()) for f in sentences if f.strip()]


def ladder_rows(text):
    """(idx, rows, problem) of the Epic's `## Value ladder` (or the old
    `## Escada de valor`) table. `idx` maps the canonical column key to its
    position; `rows` are the data rows as lists of cells (separator rows
    dropped). `problem` is None, "section" (no ladder section) or "table"
    (section without a table)."""
    marks = list(RE_SECTION.finditer(text))
    ladder = None
    for i, s in enumerate(marks):
        if s.group(1).strip().lower().startswith(("value ladder",
                                                  "escada de valor")):
            end = marks[i + 1].start() if i + 1 < len(marks) else len(text)
            ladder = text[s.end():end]
            break
    if ladder is None:
        return {}, [], "section"
    lines = [l for l in ladder.splitlines() if l.strip().startswith("|")]
    if not lines:
        return {}, [], "table"
    header_cells = [c.lower() for c in row_cells(lines[0])]
    idx = {}
    for keys, _ in QUEUE_COLUMNS:
        pos = [i for i, c in enumerate(header_cells) if c.startswith(keys)]
        if pos:
            idx[CANONICAL_COLUMN[keys]] = pos[0]
    rows = [row_cells(l) for l in lines[1:]
            if not re.fullmatch(r"[\s|:\-]*", l)]
    return idx, rows, None


def items_from_epic(text, cycle, path):
    """(demonstrates, items, warnings, error). One item per sentence of "O que
    atravessa" of the requested cycle, in text order; the cycle's script becomes
    the queue's `demonstrates:`.

    The acceptance criterion of each item is the cycle's script, because that
    is what the Epic declares as acceptance ("o roteiro de demonstração de cada
    ciclo"); the surface comes from the effect columns. No piece gets an
    acceptance criterion of its own invented here: what the Epic wrote (the
    `CA-` criteria the piece cites) is carried, nothing else.

    The script is charged whole in a last item, `C<N>-R`, blocked by every
    piece; a piece with `[espera: ...]` is born with the condition in
    `human_pending` (see the note above RE_WAIT).
    """
    warnings = []
    m = re.search(r"^\*\*Status:\*\*\s*([^\s·*]+)", text, re.M)
    status = m.group(1) if m else None
    if status not in ("ready", "closed", "pronta", "ready-to-build",
                      "pronta-para-construir"):
        warnings.append(f"o Epic está com `Status: {status}` — só `ready` passou "
                      "pelo crivo do /common:epic (todo ciclo com roteiro e "
                      "efeito observável em tela e em backend)")
    open_items = len(re.findall(r"^-\s+\[ \]", text, re.M))
    if open_items:
        warnings.append(f"{open_items} pergunta(s) ainda em aberto no Epic")

    idx, rows, problem = ladder_rows(text)
    if problem == "section":
        return None, [], warnings, (f"{path} não tem a seção `## Value "
                                  "ladder` — sem ciclo não há fila a derivar")
    if problem == "table":
        return None, [], warnings, ("a `## Value ladder` não tem tabela — "
                                  "sem ciclo não há fila a derivar")
    missing_cols = [name for keys, name in QUEUE_COLUMNS
              if CANONICAL_COLUMN[keys] in REQUIRED_COLUMNS
              and CANONICAL_COLUMN[keys] not in idx]
    if missing_cols:
        return None, [], warnings, ("a `## Value ladder` não tem a(s) "
                                  f"coluna(s) {', '.join(missing_cols)}")

    cycle_row, names = None, []
    for cells in rows:
        label = cells[idx["ciclo"]] if idx["ciclo"] < len(cells) else ""
        names.append(label)
        n = re.match(r"\D*?(\d+)", label)
        if n and int(n.group(1)) == cycle:
            cycle_row = cells
            break
    if cycle_row is None:
        return None, [], warnings, (f"o Epic não tem o ciclo {cycle} na escada "
                                  f"de valor (ciclos: {', '.join(names) or 'nenhum'})")

    def value(key):
        i = idx.get(key)
        v = cycle_row[i] if i is not None and i < len(cycle_row) else ""
        return "" if v.lower() in EMPTY_CELL else " ".join(v.split())

    label = value("ciclo") or str(cycle)
    script = value("roteiro")
    if not script:
        return None, [], warnings, (f"o ciclo \"{label}\" não tem roteiro de "
                                  "demonstração — a fila não teria o que demonstrar")
    sentences = sentences_of(value("o que atravessa"))
    if not sentences:
        return None, [], warnings, (f"o ciclo \"{label}\" tem a coluna \"What it "
                                  "crosses\" vazia — não há peça a virar item")

    screen, backend = value("efeito em tela"), value("efeito em backend")
    if screen or backend:
        surface = "; ".join(p for p in (
            f"tela: {screen}" if screen else "", f"backend: {backend}" if backend else "")
            if p)
    else:
        surface = ("não declarada no Epic (a escada não tem \"Effect on "
                      "screen\" nem \"Effect in backend\" para este ciclo; quem "
                      "pergunta é o /common:epic)")
        warnings.append(f"o ciclo \"{label}\" não declara \"Effect on screen\" nem "
                      "\"Effect in backend\" — cada item nasce com a superfície "
                      "\"não declarada\"")

    criteria = {cid: body for cid, body in RE_EPIC_CRITERION.findall(text)}
    crosses_all = "\n".join(
        cells[idx["o que atravessa"]] for cells in rows
        if idx["o que atravessa"] < len(cells))
    cited_anywhere = set(RE_CRITERION_ID.findall(crosses_all))
    orphans = [cid for cid, body in criteria.items()
               if cid not in cited_anywhere and OUT_OF_LADDER not in body.lower()]
    if orphans:
        shown = ", ".join(orphans[:8]) + (
            f" e mais {len(orphans) - 8}" if len(orphans) > 8 else "")
        warnings.append(
            f"{len(orphans)} critério(s) do Epic sem peça em \"What it "
            f"crosses\" de nenhum ciclo ({shown}) — a fila lê só essa coluna, "
            "então nenhum item os entrega; cite o id na peça ou marque `fora "
            "da escada` na linha do critério, pelo /common:epic")
    # Only the new status words: the old `pronta`/`rascunho` Epic predates the
    # walk, the same line the gate draws.
    if status in ("ready", "closed", "draft") and not any(
            sec.group(1).strip().lower().startswith(
                ("script walk", "passos do roteiro"))
            for sec in RE_SECTION.finditer(text)):
        warnings.append(
            "o Epic não tem `## Script walk` — nada conferiu que as peças "
            "somam o roteiro nem que existe peça para a chamada entre dois "
            "repositórios; quem pergunta é o /common:epic")

    script_id = script_item_id(cycle)
    items = []
    for k, sentence in enumerate(sentences, 1):
        waits = [" ".join(w.split()) for w in RE_WAIT.findall(sentence)]
        title = " ".join(RE_WAIT.sub("", sentence).split())
        why = [
            f"peça {k} de {len(sentences)} do ciclo \"{label}\" do Epic "
            f"{path}",
            INHERITED_EPIC,
            f"critério de aceite: o roteiro do ciclo — {script}",
            f"superfície onde se observa: {surface}",
            f"a peça sozinha não cumpre o roteiro: ele é cobrado inteiro no "
            f"item {script_id}"]
        cited = [c for c in dict.fromkeys(RE_CRITERION_ID.findall(sentence))
                 if c in criteria]
        if cited:
            why.append("critérios do Epic que esta peça entrega: " + "; ".join(
                f"{c}: {shorten(criteria[c])}" for c in cited))
        items.append({
            "id": f"C{cycle}-{k}",
            "title": title,
            "why": " · ".join(why),
            "status": "pending",
            "blocked_by": [],
            "human_pending": "; ".join(w for w in waits if w) or None,
        })
    items.append({
        "id": script_id,
        "title": SCRIPT_ITEM_TITLE,
        "why": " · ".join((
            f"demonstração do ciclo \"{label}\" do Epic {path}",
            "último da fila e bloqueado por todas as peças: as peças foram "
            "escritas por componente e este é o único item que cobra a "
            "ligação entre elas",
            f"critério de aceite: o roteiro do ciclo, executado de ponta a "
            f"ponta sobre dado real e não peça a peça — {script}",
            f"superfície onde se observa: {surface}",
            "o que o roteiro pedir e nenhuma peça entregar vira item novo "
            "antes deste, com o motivo")),
        "status": "pending",
        "blocked_by": [i["id"] for i in items],
        "human_pending": None,
    })
    return script, items, warnings, None


def read_epic(path, cycle):
    """(demonstrates, items, source-label) or None after reporting the error."""
    p = Path(path)
    if not p.is_file():
        print(f"{p} não existe", file=sys.stderr)
        return None
    demonstrates, items, warnings, error = items_from_epic(
        p.read_text(encoding="utf-8"), cycle, path)
    for a in warnings:
        print(f"aviso: {a}", file=sys.stderr)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return None
    source = (f"{path}, ciclo {cycle} ({len(items) - 1} peças de \"O que "
             "atravessa\"; ordem herdada do texto; mais o roteiro do ciclo "
             f"como item final, {script_item_id(cycle)})")
    return demonstrates, items, source


def cmd_from_epic(path, cycle):
    read_result = read_epic(path, cycle)
    if read_result is None:
        return 2
    demonstrates, items, _ = read_result
    print(json.dumps({"demonstrates": demonstrates, "items": items},
                     ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
    return 0


# ── reading the handoff of a /board-flow:triage triage ───────────────────────

# The five destinations the triage gives a card. The names are the bucket's in
# `/board-flow:triage`, in lowercase — translating here would create a second
# vocabulary for the same thing.
BUCKETS = ("ready", "implemented", "obsolete", "needs-refinement", "needs-decision")


def items_from_triage(handoff):
    """(items, warnings, errors). The classification is the triage's; the queue is ours.

    Each refusal below locks a rule that today only exists as prose in
    `board-flow/commands/triage.md` — and command prose erodes silently, which
    is the lesson the completeness auditor left on step 1: a `grep` on the
    instruction proves the command PROMISES to apply the rule, never that an
    execution applied it.
    """
    warnings, errors = [], []
    if not isinstance(handoff, dict):
        return [], [], ["o repasse da triagem tem que ser um objeto JSON com "
                        "`cards:` — veja `cepa-plan from-triage --exemplo`"]
    cards = handoff.get("cards")
    if not isinstance(cards, list) or not cards:
        return [], [], ["o repasse não traz nenhum card em `cards:` — uma "
                        "triagem que classificou zero cards não tem ordem a "
                        "gravar"]

    items = []
    no_why, no_reason, bad_buckets, in_grill = [], [], [], []
    out_of_queue = {"implemented": [], "needs-refinement": []}

    for i, c in enumerate(cards):
        if not isinstance(c, dict):
            errors.append(f"o card na posição {i + 1} não é um objeto")
            continue
        key = str(c.get("key") or c.get("id") or "").strip()
        if not key:
            errors.append(f"o card na posição {i + 1} não tem `key` — é por ela "
                         "que o `blocked_by` e o /common:next apontam")
            continue
        bucket = str(c.get("bucket") or "").strip().lower()
        if bucket not in BUCKETS:
            bad_buckets.append(f"{key} (`{bucket or 'vazio'}`)")
            continue

        # A NEEDS-DECISION that gets here is step 6's grill left unfinished.
        # triage.md itself says: "A NEEDS-DECISION card always leaves the
        # grill as IMPLEMENTED / READY / OBSOLETE / stays". Writing it like
        # this would hide a question nobody answered inside a queue that reads
        # as decided.
        if bucket == "needs-decision":
            in_grill.append(key)
            continue

        # Only `→ To Do` becomes a `pending` item. A card routed to In Review
        # belongs to the PROOF queue, not the build one — mixing the two makes
        # /common:next order building what is already built.
        if bucket in out_of_queue:
            out_of_queue[bucket].append(key)
            continue

        title = str(c.get("title") or c.get("summary") or "").strip()
        if not title:
            errors.append(f"{key} não tem `title`")
            continue

        if bucket == "ready":
            because = " ".join(str(c.get("why") or "").split())
            if not because:
                no_why.append(key)
                continue
            items.append({
                "id": key,
                "title": title,
                "why": because,
                "status": "pending",
                "blocked_by": [str(x) for x in (c.get("blocked_by") or [])],
                "human_pending": None,
            })
        else:  # obsolete
            reason = " ".join(str(c.get("reason") or c.get("why") or "").split())
            if not reason:
                no_reason.append(key)
                continue
            items.append({
                "id": key,
                "title": title,
                # The card leaves the queue, but the document keeps explaining
                # why: a deleted item becomes a demand the next sweep proposes
                # again, and the decision to discard is lost.
                "why": f"descartado na triagem: {reason}",
                "status": "dropped",
                "blocked_by": [],
                "human_pending": None,
                "evidence": reason,
            })

    if bad_buckets:
        errors.append("card com balde que a triagem não usa: "
                     + ", ".join(bad_buckets)
                     + f" — os válidos são {', '.join(BUCKETS)}")
    if in_grill:
        errors.append(f"{len(in_grill)} card(s) ainda em `needs-decision`: "
                     + ", ".join(in_grill)
                     + " — a grelha do passo 6 do /board-flow:triage não "
                       "terminou. Card que sai da grelha sai como ready, "
                       "implemented ou obsolete, nunca ainda em dúvida; gravar "
                       "assim esconde uma pergunta aberta dentro de uma fila "
                       "que se lê como decidida.")
    if no_why:
        errors.append(f"{len(no_why)} card READY sem `why`: " + ", ".join(no_why)
                     + " — a ordem sem o critério que a escolheu é o que o Jira "
                       "já guarda, e é exatamente o que esta fila existe para "
                       "acrescentar. Peça o motivo de cada posição em vez de "
                       "inventar um plausível.")
    if no_reason:
        errors.append(f"{len(no_reason)} card OBSOLETE sem `reason`: "
                     + ", ".join(no_reason)
                     + " — descarte sem motivo registrado é card que reaparece "
                       "na próxima varredura.")

    if not errors and not items:
        errors.append("nenhum card virou item: a triagem não deixou nenhum "
                     "READY nem nenhum OBSOLETE. Não há fila a gravar (os "
                     "IMPLEMENTED vão para /board-flow:prove-drain).")

    # A `blocked_by` pointing to a card the triage took out of the queue (went to
    # In Review, or stayed in the backlog) is not a phantom id: it is a real
    # dependency on a card that simply is not an item of THIS queue. Refusing
    # would force the agent to erase the information by hand; keeping it would
    # make the general validation refuse the whole queue for a nonexistent id.
    # It leaves the field and that is STATED — leaving silently is how a
    # dependency becomes a surprise during execution.
    outside = {k for ks in out_of_queue.values() for k in ks}
    for it in items:
        cut = [b for b in it["blocked_by"] if b in outside]
        if cut:
            it["blocked_by"] = [b for b in it["blocked_by"] if b not in outside]
            warnings.append(
                f"{it['id']} dependia de {', '.join(cut)}, que a triagem "
                "tirou desta fila (foram para a fila de prova ou ficaram no "
                "backlog) — a dependência saiu do `blocked_by` porque o "
                "/common:next só sabe esperar por item da própria fila. Se ela "
                "ainda vale, ela agora é sua para vigiar.")

    for bucket, keys in out_of_queue.items():
        if keys:
            destination = ("a fila de prova (/board-flow:prove-drain)"
                       if bucket == "implemented"
                       else "o backlog, sem mudança")
            warnings.append(f"{len(keys)} card(s) `{bucket}` ficaram FORA da "
                          f"fila, por desenho — o destino deles é {destination}: "
                          + ", ".join(keys))

    # Truncation is never silent: a queue covering 15 of 27 cards reads, months
    # later, as the whole board's queue.
    rest = handoff.get("remaining_in_column")
    if isinstance(rest, int) and rest > 0:
        warnings.append(f"a triagem parou no teto e deixou {rest} card(s) na "
                      "coluna sem classificar — esta fila é um pedaço do "
                      "quadro, não o quadro. Está dito na linha `source`.")

    return items, warnings, errors


def triage_source(handoff):
    """The plan's `source` line, assembled from what the triage itself recorded."""
    p = []
    key = handoff.get("project_key")
    p.append(f"Jira {key}" if key else "Jira")
    if handoff.get("source_column"):
        p.append(f"coluna {handoff['source_column']}")
    if handoff.get("scope"):
        p.append(f"escopo {handoff['scope']}")
    if handoff.get("triaged_on"):
        p.append(f"triado em {handoff['triaged_on']}")
    text = " · ".join(p) + " (classificado por /board-flow:triage)"
    rest = handoff.get("remaining_in_column")
    if isinstance(rest, int) and rest > 0:
        text += (f" — PARCIAL: {rest} card(s) da coluna ficaram sem "
                  "classificar neste run")
    return text


def read_handoff(path):
    """(handoff, error). JSON/YAML file or '-' for stdin."""
    try:
        raw = sys.stdin.read() if path == "-" else Path(path).read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except OSError as e:
        return None, f"não deu para ler {path}: {e}"
    if not raw.strip():
        return None, f"{path} veio vazio"
    try:
        return json.loads(raw), None
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        try:
            return yaml.safe_load(raw), None
        except yaml.YAMLError as e:
            return None, f"{path} não é JSON nem YAML válido ({e})"


def cmd_from_triage(path, as_json=True):
    handoff, error = read_handoff(path)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    items, warnings, errors = items_from_triage(handoff)
    for a in warnings:
        print(f"aviso: {a}", file=sys.stderr)
    if errors:
        for e in errors:
            print(f"recusa: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    gaps = validate_items(items)
    if gaps:
        print(f"{len(gaps)} lacuna(s) nos itens que a triagem produziu",
              file=sys.stderr)
        for f in gaps:
            print(f"  - {f}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    print(json.dumps(items, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) if as_json else items)
    return 0

# ── the batch: what /common:drain-plan can execute NOW ───────────────────────

# What STOPS the batch. `human_pending`, `in_progress` and `blocked-before`
# left here: all three DEFER the item and let the following ones run.
STOPS = ("end-of-queue", "cap", "blocked")
DEFERRALS = ("human_pending", "reserved", "depends-on-deferred",
              "blocked-before")

# Transition window (same method as f26a765/84fde4d): the English value is what
# is emitted; the old Portuguese spelling is accepted by readers and still
# carried in `reason_pt`. Drop this map once no reader or .jsonl needs the old.
REASON_ALIASES = {
    "fim-da-fila": "end-of-queue",
    "teto": "cap",
    "bloqueado": "blocked",
    "reservado": "reserved",
    "depende-de-adiado": "depends-on-deferred",
    "bloqueado-antes": "blocked-before",
}
REASON_PT = {new: old for old, new in REASON_ALIASES.items()}


def reason_alias(value):
    """Old Portuguese stop/deferral reason -> the English one (unknown: as is)."""
    return REASON_ALIASES.get(value, value)


def reason_pt(value):
    """The old Portuguese spelling of an English reason (unknown: as is)."""
    return REASON_PT.get(reason_alias(value), value)


def build_batch(items, max_items, reservation_state=reservation_of):
    """(batch, stop, warnings, deferred) — what runs now, IN QUEUE ORDER.

    `stop["reason"]` and each `deferred[]["reason"]` carry the ENGLISH value
    (end-of-queue, cap, blocked / reserved, depends-on-deferred, blocked-before,
    human_pending). During the transition window both also carry `reason_pt`,
    the old Portuguese spelling (fim-da-fila, teto, bloqueado, reservado,
    depende-de-adiado, bloqueado-antes), for readers not yet updated.

    The order is the document's data, so this function never reorders and never
    promotes an item ahead of another. What it does, since 2026-08-28, is
    distinguish two things that used to be the same:

      - **stop** the batch — what comes after is not executable while that is
        unresolved, and continuing would spend budget on the same jam;
      - **defer** an item — it does not run now, but does not block the
        following ones. The item leaves this batch and returns in the next
        `queue`, and the ORDER written in `plan.yaml` is not touched: deferring
        is an execution decision, reordering belongs to `/common:queue`.

    What DEFERS (owner's decision, 2026-08-28 — before that the first two
    stopped the whole batch):

      - open `human_pending` — only the human closes the route, and jamming
        the queue until they return is what turned a batch of 3 into a batch
        of 1. The debt does not vanish: the item is deferred with the route
        verbatim, and the batch report collects them all at the end.
      - `in_progress` with a LIVE owner — another session is on it right now.
        Here the deferral says WHO, which the old stop could not say.
      - `blocked` from a previous run — an outside condition nobody touched.
        Re-executing measures the same jam, so the item does not run; but
        jamming the whole queue behind it is worse, and in an unattended window
        (`cepa-until`) it costs the whole night. Owner's decision, 2026-08-30,
        revisiting the /board-flow:drain heritage: the item is deferred with the
        reason verbatim and the end report collects them all.
      - item that depends (`blocked_by`) on an item DEFERRED in this pass — the
        cascade. Without it, deferring B would make C stop the batch because
        of the dependency, and the deferral would have served no purpose.

    What still STOPS:

      - `blocked` by an item that is neither done nor in the batch — copied
        from `/board-flow:drain`: stuck work is not pushed.
      - `cap` — the `--max`. Each item here is a whole build with an
        acceptance and proof gate.

    And what RECOVERS: an `in_progress` whose owning session no longer exists is
    an orphan reservation (dead run). It becomes executable again, with a
    warning — the alternative is the queue jamming forever because of a session
    that ended.

    A `blocked_by` pointing to an item ALREADY CHOSEN in this batch does not
    block: it will close first, because the list order is respected. Without
    this the batch would always have at most one item in any queue with chained
    dependencies.
    """
    warnings, deferred = [], []
    resolved = {str(it.get("id")) for it in items
                  if isinstance(it, dict) and status_of(it) in ("done", "dropped")}
    dropped_ids = {str(it.get("id")) for it in items
                if isinstance(it, dict) and status_of(it) == "dropped"}
    deferred_ids = set()

    def defer(ident, it, reason, detail):
        deferred_ids.add(ident)
        deferred.append({"id": ident, "title": it.get("title"),
                        "reason": reason, "reason_pt": reason_pt(reason),
                        "detail": detail,
                        "question": it.get("owner_question"),
                        "owner_summary": it.get("owner_summary"),
                        "human_pending": it.get("human_pending"),
                        "evidence": it.get("evidence")})

    batch, stop = [], {"reason": "end-of-queue", "reason_pt": "fim-da-fila",
                        "item": None, "detail":
                        "a fila acabou — nenhum item pendente sobrou"}
    for it in items:
        if not isinstance(it, dict):
            continue
        ident, st = str(it.get("id")), status_of(it)
        if st in ("done", "dropped"):
            continue
        if st == "in_progress":
            state, detail = reservation_state(it)
            if state == "orfa":
                warnings.append(
                    f"{ident} estava `in_progress` mas a reserva é órfã: "
                    f"{detail}. Tratei como executável — o `start` reivindica "
                    "a reserva antes de qualquer trabalho.")
            else:
                defer(ident, it, "reserved", f"{ident}: {detail}")
                continue
        if st == "blocked":
            reason = str(it.get("evidence") or "").strip()
            defer(ident, it, "blocked-before",
                 f"{ident} saiu `blocked` de um run anterior"
                 + (f": {reason}" if reason else " (sem motivo registrado)")
                 + ". Não re-executo — enquanto a condição de fora não mudar, "
                 "seria o mesmo travamento; devolver o item para `pending` é de "
                 "quem resolveu a condição. Mas ele também não para os "
                 "seguintes")
            continue
        if it.get("human_pending") is not None:
            defer(ident, it, "human_pending",
                 f"{ident} tem uma rota que só você fecha: {it['human_pending']}")
            continue
        waiting = [str(b) for b in (it.get("blocked_by") or [])
                     if str(b) in deferred_ids]
        if waiting:
            defer(ident, it, "depends-on-deferred",
                 f"{ident} depende de {', '.join(waiting)}, que ficou de fora "
                 "deste lote — executá-lo agora seria construir sobre o que não "
                 "fechou")
            continue
        pending_deps = [b for b in (it.get("blocked_by") or [])
                     if str(b) not in resolved
                     and str(b) not in {x["id"] for x in batch}]
        if pending_deps:
            stop = {"reason": "blocked", "reason_pt": "bloqueado",
                    "item": ident, "detail":
                      f"{ident} depende de {', '.join(pending_deps)}, que não "
                      "está feito nem entra neste lote"}
            break
        for b in (it.get("blocked_by") or []):
            if str(b) in dropped_ids:
                warnings.append(
                    f"{ident} depende de {b}, que está `dropped` — ninguém vai "
                    "fechar esse item, então a dependência não está satisfeita, "
                    "está abandonada. Tratei como resolvida para o item não "
                    "ficar preso para sempre; confira se ela ainda vale.")
        if len(batch) >= max_items:
            stop = {"reason": "cap", "reason_pt": "teto",
                    "item": ident, "detail":
                      f"o teto --max {max_items} foi atingido; {ident} seria o "
                      "próximo"}
            break
        batch.append({"id": ident, "title": it.get("title"), "why": it.get("why"),
                     "blocked_by": [str(b) for b in (it.get("blocked_by") or [])]})

    if reason_alias(stop["reason"]) == "end-of-queue" and deferred:
        stop["detail"] = (
            f"a fila acabou — nenhum item executável sobrou, e {len(deferred)} "
            "ficaram adiados (cada um com o motivo, no relatório)")
    return batch, stop, warnings, deferred


def batch_summary(items, batch, stop, deferred=()):
    count = {"pending": 0, "in_progress": 0, "done": 0, "blocked": 0, "dropped": 0}
    for it in items:
        if isinstance(it, dict):
            count[status_of(it)] = count.get(status_of(it), 0) + 1
    remaining = count["pending"] - len(batch)
    return {"por_status": count, "no_lote": len(batch),
            "adiados": len(deferred),
            "pendentes_fora_do_lote": max(remaining, 0)}


def cmd_queue(root, name, max_items, as_json):
    target = queue_path(root, name)
    if not target.is_file():
        print(f"{target} não existe — não há fila para executar. Quem escreve é "
              "o /common:queue.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    plan, error = read_plan(target)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if mode_of(plan) != MODE:
        print(f"COLISÃO: {target} é um plano '{mode_of(plan)}' — ondas do "
              "/maestro:program-plan, que quem executa é o /maestro:run. Este "
              "lote só sabe fila.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    gaps = validate_plan(plan)
    if gaps:
        print(f"{target}: {len(gaps)} lacuna(s) — não dá para montar lote sobre "
              "uma fila inválida", file=sys.stderr)
        for f in gaps:
            print(f"  - {f}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    items = plan.get("items") or []
    batch, stop, warnings, deferred = build_batch(
        items, max_items,
        reservation_state=lambda it: reservation_of(it, root))
    output = {"program": qp.queue_name_of(plan), "queue": qp.queue_name_of(plan),
             "path": str(target), "max": max_items,
             "batch": batch, "stop": stop, "deferred": deferred,
             "warnings": warnings,
             "totals": batch_summary(items, batch, stop, deferred)}
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(output, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
        return 0

    print(f"fila {output['queue']} · {target}")
    if not batch:
        print("  lote VAZIO — nada a executar agora")
    for i, it in enumerate(batch, 1):
        print(f"  {i}. {it['id']} — {it['title']}")
        print(f"     porque: {it['why']}")
    for ad in deferred:
        print(f"  adiado: {ad['id']} ({ad['reason']}) — {ad['detail']}")
    print(f"  parada: {stop['reason']} — {stop['detail']}")
    for a in warnings:
        print(f"  aviso: {a}")
    t = output["totals"]
    print(f"  {t['no_lote']} no lote · {t['adiados']} adiado(s) · "
          f"{t['pendentes_fora_do_lote']} pendente(s) fora dele · "
          f"{t['por_status'].get('done', 0)} done")
    return 0


# ── status: the whole queue, read-only ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# `queue` answers "what does the next batch execute" and so hides what already
# closed and stops at the first jam. `/common:next` points at ONE step. Neither
# answers "how is the queue right now?", and on 2026-09-28 the owner asked
# exactly that and there was no command: only opening the 72-item YAML by hand.

STATUS_GROUPS = (
    ("in_progress", "em andamento"),
    ("pending", "pendentes"),
    ("blocked", "bloqueados"),
    ("done", "concluídos"),
    ("dropped", "descartados"),
)


def single_track_queues(root):
    """The names of the repo's single-track queues, in alphabetical order."""
    names = []
    for name, qfile in qp.queue_files(root):
        plan, error = read_plan(qfile)
        if not error and isinstance(plan, dict) and mode_of(plan) == MODE:
            names.append(name)
    return names


# ── where the item's code is, asked to git ───────────────────────────────────
#
# `evidence` is prose written once and it goes stale (owner, 2026-11-10,
# fb-20261110-1): C1-17 of wego-digitacao-backend said "sem merge" after the
# merge, and C1-18 of wego-faturamento-backend had 19 commits on a branch the
# committed queue never named. So `status` asks git where the code cited by
# the item is, instead of repeating the text.

SHA_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![0-9A-Za-z])(?=[0-9a-f]*[0-9])[0-9a-f]{7,40}(?![0-9A-Za-z])")


def main_branch(root):
    """The ref `status` calls main: the local main (what is merged here),
    else master, else the remote's."""
    for ref in ("main", "master", "origin/HEAD", "origin/main"):
        rc, out, _ = _git(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", ref + "^{commit}")
        if rc == 0 and out.strip():
            return ref
    return None


def local_branches(root):
    rc, out, _ = _git(root, "for-each-ref", "--format=%(refname:short)", "refs/heads")
    return out.split() if rc == 0 else []


def _id_in(ident, text):
    return bool(ident) and re.search(
        rf"(?<![A-Za-z0-9]){re.escape(ident)}(?![A-Za-z0-9])", text, re.I) is not None


def _unmerged(root, ref, head, limit=None):
    """How many commits of `head` (after `limit`) have no equivalent change in
    `ref`. `git cherry` and not `rev-list`: a cherry-pick into main (C1-12 of
    wego-faturamento-backend) is in main under another hash."""
    rc, out, _ = _git(root, "cherry", ref, head, *([limit] if limit else []))
    if rc != 0:
        rc, out, _ = _git(root, "rev-list", "--count", f"{ref}..{head}")
        return int(out.strip()) if rc == 0 and out.strip().isdigit() else 0
    return sum(1 for line in out.splitlines() if line.startswith("+"))


def code_location(root, it, ref, branches):
    """{"ref", "fora", "no_main"} for the commits and branches the item points
    at, or None when it points at nothing that exists in this repo.

    Cited: a commit in `evidence`, `owner_summary` or `head_commit`; a branch
    named in that text, the reservation's branch, or a local branch whose name
    carries the item id as a whole token (the C1-18 branch the queue never
    named). A branch counts as outside main when it has commits main lacks."""
    text = " ".join(str(it.get(k) or "") for k in ("evidence", "owner_summary"))
    ident = str(it.get("id") or "")
    claimed = (it.get("claimed_by") or {}).get("branch")
    base = ref.split("/")[-1]
    cited = [b for b in branches
             if b not in (ref, base, "main", "master")
             and (b == claimed or _id_in(ident, b)
                  or re.search(rf"(?<![\w/.-]){re.escape(b)}(?![\w/-])", text))]
    fora, no_main, off_branches = [], [], []
    for b in cited:
        n = _unmerged(root, ref, b)
        if n:
            fora.append(f"{b} (+{n} commit{'s' if n > 1 else ''})")
            off_branches.append(b)
        else:
            no_main.append(b)
    seen = set()
    for sha in (SHA_RE.findall(text)
                + ([str(it["head_commit"])] if it.get("head_commit") else [])):
        rc, out, _ = _git(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", sha + "^{commit}")
        full = out.strip()
        if rc != 0 or not full or full in seen:
            continue
        seen.add(full)
        if (_git(root, "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", full, ref)[0] == 0
                or not _unmerged(root, ref, full, full + "~1")):
            no_main.append(sha[:12])
        elif not any(_git(root, "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", full, b)[0] == 0
                     for b in off_branches):
            fora.append(sha[:12])
    if not fora and not no_main:
        return None
    return {"ref": ref, "fora": fora, "no_main": no_main}


def code_line(codigo):
    """The status line, or None: only what is outside main is news."""
    if not codigo or not codigo["fora"]:
        return None
    return f"código fora do {codigo['ref']}: " + ", ".join(codigo["fora"])


def sem_epic(it):
    """The item entered by `cepa-plan add`, so its domain decisions never went
    through /common:epic (owner, 2026-11-10: C1-17 and C1-18). Older items
    carry no flag; the phrase `add` writes into `why` gives them away."""
    return it.get("sem_epic") is True or NOT_PRIORITIZED_PHRASE in str(it.get("why") or "")


SEM_EPIC_LINE = "sem Epic: entrou por cepa-plan add, as decisões de domínio não passaram pelo /common:epic"
PEGAVEL_LINE = "pegável: não conta como pronto, mas o próximo cepa-until pega mesmo sem Epic"


def first_sentence(text, limit=160):
    t = " ".join(str(text or "").split())
    if len(t) <= limit:
        return t
    return t[:limit - 1].rstrip() + "…"


def owner_lines(lines, queue):
    """The summary under the scoreboard: how many `pending` a run would take,
    and what waits on the owner, split by kind. The old single line ("43 com
    ação humana aberta") mixed 6 items that hold the queue with 37 delivered
    ones carrying a leftover task, and gave no way to answer them."""
    pending = [l for l in lines if l["status"] == "pending"]
    ready = [l for l in pending if l["pronto"]]
    loose = [l for l in pending if l["sem_epic"]]
    out = [f"{len(ready)} de {len(pending)} pendentes prontos para o agente"
           + (": " + ", ".join(str(l["id"]) for l in ready) if ready else "")
           + ("; os outros esperam você ou outro item"
              if len(ready) + len(loose) < len(pending) else "")]
    if loose:
        out.append(f"{len(loose)} sem Epic à parte: "
                   + ", ".join(str(l["id"]) for l in loose)
                   + " (entraram por cepa-plan add; o cepa-until pega os prontos, "
                   "mas as decisões de domínio não passaram pelo /common:epic)")
    holding = [l for l in lines if l["status"] not in ("done", "dropped")
               and (l["human_pending"] is not None or l["status"] == "blocked")]
    leftover = [l for l in lines if l["status"] == "done"
                and l["human_pending"] is not None]
    if holding or leftover:
        out.append(f"esperam você: {len(holding)} itens parados"
                   + (f" ({', '.join(str(l['id']) for l in holding)})" if holding else "")
                   + f" e {len(leftover)} tarefas que sobraram em itens "
                   f"concluídos. Responda uma por uma: cepa-until decide {queue}")
    return out


def cmd_status(root, name, status_filter, as_json, item_id=None, via_show=False):
    if not name:
        names = single_track_queues(root)
        if not names:
            print(f"nenhuma fila em {root / qp.NEW_DIR} — quem "
                  "escreve é o /common:queue", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        if len(names) > 1:
            print("há mais de uma fila; diga qual: " + ", ".join(names),
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        name = names[0]
    target = queue_path(root, name)
    if not target.is_file():
        print(f"{target} não existe — quem escreve a fila é o /common:queue",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    plan, error = read_plan(target)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if mode_of(plan) != MODE:
        print(f"COLISÃO: {target} é um plano '{mode_of(plan)}' — ondas do "
              "/maestro:program-plan, não uma fila", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3

    items = plan.get("items") or []
    # "Pendente" is not "pronto": a `pending` with an open human route, or
    # waiting on an item that will not close, is skipped by every run. Ready
    # is what `build_batch` would hand a run now, with no ceiling (owner,
    # 2026-11-02: "o cepa-until não deve perder tempo em itens que certamente
    # não irão avançar"). Derived, never stored: a stored flag goes stale.
    ready_ids = {b["id"] for b in build_batch(
        items, 10 ** 6,
        reservation_state=lambda it: reservation_of(it, root))[0]}
    ref = main_branch(root)
    branches = local_branches(root) if ref else []
    lines = []
    for pos, it in enumerate(items, 1):
        owner = it.get("claimed_by") or {}
        lines.append({
            # `pronto` leaves out the items with no Epic (owner, 2026-11-10);
            # `pegavel` is still what build_batch hands a run, Epic or not.
            "pronto": str(it.get("id")) in ready_ids and not sem_epic(it),
            "pegavel": str(it.get("id")) in ready_ids,
            "sem_epic": sem_epic(it),
            "codigo": (code_location(root, it, ref, branches)
                       if ref and status_of(it) != "dropped" else None),
            "posicao": pos, "id": it.get("id"), "title": it.get("title"),
            "status": status_of(it), "why": it.get("why"),
            "blocked_by": it.get("blocked_by") or [],
            "human_pending": it.get("human_pending"),
            "evidence": it.get("evidence"),
            "owner_summary": it.get("owner_summary"),
            "claimed_by": ({"session_id": owner.get("session_id"),
                            "branch": owner.get("branch"),
                            "started_at": owner.get("started_at")}
                           if owner else None),
        })
    counts = {st: sum(1 for l in lines if l["status"] == st)
                for st in STATUSES}
    visible = [l for l in lines if not status_filter or l["status"] == status_filter]

    if item_id is not None:
        # One item, every field, nothing cut: the list view trims the human
        # action and the reason with "…" (owner, 2026-11-05: "Como eu vejo
        # detalhes de cada item?").
        found = [l for l in lines if str(l["id"]) == item_id]
        if not found:
            print(f"item {item_id} não existe na fila "
                  f"{qp.queue_name_of(plan, name)}; ids: "
                  + ", ".join(str(l["id"]) for l in lines), file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        if not via_show:
            print(f"dica: cepa plan show {name} {item_id} é o nome deste "
                  "comando; status <fila> <id> segue como atalho",
                  file=sys.stderr)
        return item_detail(qp.queue_name_of(plan, name), target,
                           found[0], as_json, plan=plan, root=root)

    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"program": qp.queue_name_of(plan, name),
                          "queue": qp.queue_name_of(plan, name),
                          "path": str(target), "total": len(lines),
                          "por_status": counts,
                          "prontos": sum(1 for l in lines if l["pronto"]),
                          "sem_epic": [l["id"] for l in lines if l["sem_epic"]
                                       and l["status"] == "pending"],
                          "filtro": status_filter,
                          "items": visible}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
        return 0
    if _tui.SCREEN.enabled:
        return status_on_screen(qp.queue_name_of(plan, name), target, lines,
                              counts, visible)

    print(f"fila {qp.queue_name_of(plan, name)} · {target}")
    print("  " + " · ".join(f"{counts[st]} {grp_label}" for st, grp_label in STATUS_GROUPS)
          + f" · {len(lines)} no total")
    for text in owner_lines(lines, qp.queue_name_of(plan, name)):
        print("  " + text)
    for st, grp_label in STATUS_GROUPS:
        group = [l for l in visible if l["status"] == st]
        if not group:
            continue
        print(f"\n{grp_label} ({len(group)})")
        for l in group:
            print(f"  {l['posicao']:>3}. {l['id']} — {l['title']}")
            if code_line(l["codigo"]):
                print(f"       {code_line(l['codigo'])}")
            if st in ("done", "dropped"):
                continue
            if l["sem_epic"]:
                print(f"       {SEM_EPIC_LINE}")
            if l["pegavel"] and not l["pronto"]:
                print(f"       {PEGAVEL_LINE}")
            if l["claimed_by"]:
                c = l["claimed_by"]
                print(f"       reservado: sessão {c['session_id'] or '?'}"
                      f" desde {c['started_at'] or '?'}")
            if l["pronto"]:
                print("       pronto: o próximo cepa-until pega")
            if l["blocked_by"]:
                print(f"       espera: {', '.join(map(str, l['blocked_by']))}")
            if l["human_pending"] is not None:
                print(f"       ação humana: {first_sentence(l['human_pending'])}")
            if st == "blocked" and blocked_reason(l):
                print(f"       motivo: {blocked_reason(l)}")
    return 0



def ready_of_queue(root, name, target=None):
    """(summary, warnings, error) of one queue for `ready`.

    `error` is set, and the rest empty, when the file cannot be read: that
    queue is OUT of the list. `warnings` are build_batch's notes about a
    queue that IS in the list (orphan reservation, dependency on a dropped
    item). A waves plan is not a queue: (None, [], None) — nothing to list,
    nothing to say."""
    target = target or queue_path(root, name)
    plan, error = read_plan(target)
    if error:
        return None, [], error
    if not isinstance(plan, dict) or mode_of(plan) != MODE:
        return None, [], None
    items = [it for it in (plan.get("items") or []) if isinstance(it, dict)]
    batch, _stop, warnings, deferred = build_batch(items, 10 ** 6)
    pos = {str(it.get("id")): i for i, it in enumerate(items, 1)}
    in_batch = {b["id"] for b in batch}
    # Only a dependency that is ITSELF in this list is worth a line: one that
    # is already `done` holds nothing, and build_batch never lets a pending one
    # through.
    ready = [{"posicao": pos.get(b["id"]), "id": b["id"], "title": b["title"],
              "why": b["why"],
              "blocked_by": [d for d in b["blocked_by"] if d in in_batch]}
             for b in batch]
    pending = [it for it in items if status_of(it) == "pending"]
    waiting = [str(it.get("id")) for it in items
               if status_of(it) not in ("done", "dropped")
               and (it.get("human_pending") is not None
                    or status_of(it) == "blocked")]
    return {"queue": qp.queue_name_of(plan, name), "path": str(target),
            "prontos": ready, "pendentes": len(pending),
            "abertos": sum(1 for it in items
                           if status_of(it) not in ("done", "dropped")),
            "esperam_dono": waiting,
            "adiados": [{"id": d["id"], "reason": reason_alias(d["reason"])}
                        for d in deferred],
            }, warnings, None


def cmd_ready(root, as_json):
    # Walks the files, not `single_track_queues`: that helper drops an
    # unreadable queue in silence, and a queue that vanishes from this list
    # without a word is exactly what the owner must hear about.
    queues, unreadable = [], 0
    for name, qfile in qp.queue_files(root):
        summary, warnings, error = ready_of_queue(root, name, qfile)
        if error:
            unreadable += 1
            print(f"aviso: fila {name} ilegível, fora da lista: {error}",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            continue
        for w in warnings:
            print(f"aviso: fila {name}: {w}", file=sys.stderr)
        if summary is not None:
            queues.append(summary)
    if not queues and not unreadable:
        print(f"nenhuma fila em {root / qp.NEW_DIR} — quem escreve é o "
              "/common:queue", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    total = sum(len(q["prontos"]) for q in queues)
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"root": str(root), "filas": queues,
                          "total_prontos": total}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
        return 0
    print(f"prontos para construir · {len(queues)} filas · {total} itens")
    for q in queues:
        ready = q["prontos"]
        head = f"\nfila {q['queue']} · {len(ready)} de {q['pendentes']} pendentes prontos"
        if ready:
            print(head)
            for l in ready:
                print(f"  {l['posicao']:>3}. {l['id']} — {l['title']}")
                if l["blocked_by"]:
                    print(f"       espera: {', '.join(l['blocked_by'])} (entra "
                          "antes neste lote)")
            continue
        if q["abertos"] == 0:
            print(head + " — fila fechada: tudo concluído ou descartado")
        elif q["esperam_dono"]:
            print(head + f" — esperam você: {', '.join(q['esperam_dono'])}"
                  f" (cepa until decide {q['queue']})")
        else:
            print(head + " — nada pronto: os abertos esperam outro item ou "
                  "estão reservados")
    return 0

# ── one item in full: `cepa-plan show <fila> <id>` ──────────────────────────
#
# On 2026-11-05 the owner read item C1-15 of the kairos queue and could not tell
# what "L1 a L6" or "S11" in the title meant, nor where to look: the queue
# stores the title as the Epic wrote it and nothing else. The Epic is named in
# the queue's `source`, so the codes are resolved HERE, at read time — a field
# written per item would be stale for every queue that already exists.

CODE_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![\w-])([A-Z]{1,2})-?(\d+(?:\.\d+)?[a-z]?)(?![\w.])")
RANGE_CAP = 200  # members above which a range is only looked up as a phrase
RANGE_RE = re.compile(r"(?<![\w-])([A-Z]{1,2})(\d+) a \1(\d+)(?![\w.])")


def codes_in(text):
    """The codes a title cites, each once, the section codes (S11) first: a
    range `L1 a L6` comes as the phrase plus its six members, `CA-11.1` as
    written. Returns [(code, members)]: members is the expansion of a range,
    [] for a plain code."""
    out = []
    for m in RANGE_RE.finditer(text):
        lo, hi = int(m.group(2)), int(m.group(3))
        # A typo like "L1 a L99999999" must not expand into millions of
        # lookups (proof-reviewer, 2026-11-05: the command hung past 60s).
        members = ([f"{m.group(1)}{n}" for n in range(lo, hi + 1)]
                   if hi - lo < RANGE_CAP else [])
        out.append((m.group(0), members))
    for m in CODE_RE.finditer(text):
        out.append((m.group(1) + ("-" if "-" in m.group(0) else "") + m.group(2), []))
    seen, uniq = set(), []
    for c, members in out:
        if c not in seen:
            seen.add(c)
            uniq.append((c, members))
    uniq.sort(key=lambda cm: 0 if cm[0].startswith("S") else 1)
    return uniq


def epic_of(root, plan):
    """(path as written in `source`, lines) — lines is None when the file
    is not there or lies outside the repo, path is None when `source` names
    no .md file. A `source` with an absolute path or `..` must not turn the
    command into a reader of arbitrary files (proof-reviewer, 2026-11-05)."""
    m = re.search(r"\S+\.md", str(plan.get("source") or ""))
    if not m:
        return None, None
    rel = m.group(0).rstrip(",;:)")
    base = Path(root).resolve()
    p = (Path(rel) if Path(rel).is_absolute() else base / rel).resolve()
    if not p.is_relative_to(base):
        return rel, "fora"
    if not p.is_file():
        return rel, None
    return rel, p.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines()


def _plain(line):
    t = re.sub(r"^\s*(?:[-*]\s+|#{1,6}\s+)", "", line)
    return " ".join(t.replace("**", "").split())


def find_code(lines, code, first=(0, None)):
    """(line number, text) of where the Epic defines `code`: a heading
    (`### S11.`), a bold label (`**CA-11.1**`) or a `L1:` definition. Looks in
    `first` (a line range) before the whole file."""
    heading = re.compile(rf"^#{{1,6}}\s+{re.escape(code)}(?=[.\s:])")
    bold = re.compile(rf"\*\*{re.escape(code)}\*\*")
    defn = re.compile(rf"(?<![\w-]){re.escape(code)}:")
    ranges = [first, (0, None)] if first != (0, None) else [(0, None)]
    for pat in (heading, bold, defn):
        for lo, hi in ranges:
            for i, ln in enumerate(lines[lo:hi], lo + 1):
                if pat.search(ln):
                    return i, _plain(ln)
    return None, None


def section_range(lines, n):
    """The lines under heading number `n` (1-based) up to the next heading
    of the same or higher level."""
    level = len(lines[n - 1]) - len(lines[n - 1].lstrip("#"))
    for j in range(n, len(lines)):
        m = re.match(r"^(#{1,6})\s", lines[j])
        if m and len(m.group(1)) <= level:
            return (n, j)
    return (n, None)


def source_refs(root, plan, title):
    """What the item's title cites, resolved in the Epic the queue came from:
    {"epic": path or None, "refs": [{"code", "line", "text"}]}."""
    epic, lines = epic_of(root, plan)
    refs = []
    codes = codes_in(str(title or ""))
    if lines is None or lines == "fora":
        return {"epic": epic, "found": False, "outside_repo": lines == "fora",
                "refs": [{"code": c, "line": None, "text": None} for c, _ in codes]}
    within = (0, None)
    done = set()
    for c, members in codes:
        if c in done:
            continue
        n, text = find_code(lines, c, within)
        if n is None and members:
            # The Epic may define the range member by member (L1, L2, ...)
            # instead of as one phrase ("D1 a D8").
            for m in members:
                done.add(m)
                mn, mt = find_code(lines, m, within)
                refs.append({"code": m, "line": mn, "text": mt})
            continue
        done.update(members)
        refs.append({"code": c, "line": n, "text": text})
        if n and c.startswith("S") and within == (0, None):
            within = section_range(lines, n)
    return {"epic": epic, "found": True, "refs": refs}


def why_parts(text):
    """The `why` of a queue item written by --from-epic/--from-spec is four
    sentences glued with " · "; shown as one paragraph it is unreadable."""
    return [p.strip() for p in str(text or "").split(" · ") if p.strip()]


def evidence_parts(text):
    """Each `finish`/`answer` prepends its round and keeps the older ones
    behind "Evidência anterior:". One entry per round, newest first."""
    parts = re.split(r"\s*Evidência anterior:\s*", str(text or ""))
    return [p.strip() for p in parts if p.strip()]


def item_detail(program, target, l, as_json, plan=None, root=None):
    """`cepa-plan show <fila> <id>`: one item, every field in full, the codes of
    the title resolved in the Epic named by the queue's `source`."""
    src = source_refs(root, plan or {}, l["title"]) if plan is not None else None
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"program": program, "queue": program,
                          "path": str(target), "item": l, "source": src},
                         ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
        return 0
    label = dict(STATUS_GROUPS).get(l["status"], l["status"])
    c = l["claimed_by"]
    source_lines = []
    if src and src["epic"]:
        source_lines.append(src["epic"] + " (campo `source` da fila)")
        if src.get("outside_repo"):
            source_lines.append("Epic fora do repo: não leio arquivo fora da raiz")
        elif not src["found"]:
            source_lines.append("não achei o arquivo a partir do repo")
        for r in src["refs"]:
            if r["line"]:
                source_lines.append(f"{r['code']} · linha {r['line']} · {r['text']}")
            else:
                source_lines.append(f"{r['code']} · não achei no Epic")
    elif src is not None:
        source_lines.append("a fila não aponta um Epic em `source`; o título "
                            "vem de: " + (str((plan or {}).get("source")) or "(vazio)"))
    ev = evidence_parts(l["evidence"])
    fields = [
        ("status", [f"{l['status']} ({label})"
                    + (" · pronto: o próximo cepa-until pega" if l["pronto"]
                       else " · " + PEGAVEL_LINE if l.get("pegavel") else "")]),
        ("título", [l["title"]]),
        ("fonte", source_lines),
        ("por que nesta posição", why_parts(l["why"])),
        ("espera", [", ".join(map(str, l["blocked_by"]))] if l["blocked_by"] else []),
        ("ação humana", [l["human_pending"]] if l["human_pending"] else []),
        ("código", ([code_line(l["codigo"])] if code_line(l.get("codigo"))
                    else [f"no {l['codigo']['ref']}: " + ", ".join(l["codigo"]["no_main"])]
                    if l.get("codigo") else [])),
        ("sem Epic", [SEM_EPIC_LINE.split(": ", 1)[1]] if l.get("sem_epic") else []),
        ("evidência" + (" (mais recente primeiro)" if len(ev) > 1 else ""), ev),
        ("resumo para o dono", [l["owner_summary"]] if l["owner_summary"] else []),
        ("reservado", [f"sessão {c['session_id'] or '?'} na branch "
                       f"{c['branch'] or '?'} desde {c['started_at'] or '?'}"]
                      if c else []),
    ]
    t = _tui.SCREEN
    if t.enabled:
        print(t.header(f"fila {program} · item {l['posicao']}", str(l["id"])))
        print(t.c("cinza", f"  {target}"))
        for key, texts in fields:
            texts = [x for x in texts if x not in (None, "")]
            if not texts:
                continue
            print()
            print("  " + t.c("negrito", key))
            if len(texts) == 1:
                for x in t.wrap(" ".join(str(texts[0]).split()), 4):
                    print(x)
                continue
            for text in texts:
                for x in t.wrap("- " + " ".join(str(text).split()), 4, hanging=6):
                    print(x)
        return 0
    print(f"fila {program} · item {l['posicao']} · {l['id']}")
    for key, texts in fields:
        texts = [x for x in texts if x not in (None, "")]
        if not texts:
            continue
        if len(texts) == 1:
            print(f"\n{key}:\n  {' '.join(str(texts[0]).split())}")
            continue
        print(f"\n{key}:")
        for text in texts:
            print(f"  - {' '.join(str(text).split())}")
    return 0


# Glyph and color of each group on the terminal screen.
STATUS_VISUAL = {
    "in_progress": ("▶", "ciano"),
    "pending": ("○", "amarelo"),
    "blocked": ("■", "vermelho"),
    "done": ("✓", "verde"),
    "dropped": ("✗", "cinza"),
}


def status_on_screen(program, target, lines, counts, visible):
    """The decorated `status`, when the output is a terminal: title bar,
    scoreboard per group, progress bar, and each item with the id on one line
    and the title wrapped below. Done and dropped take a single line."""
    t = _tui.SCREEN
    w = t.width()
    total = len(lines)
    done_count = counts["done"] + counts["dropped"]
    print(t.header(f"fila {program}", f"{total} itens"))
    print(t.c("cinza", f"  {target}"))
    print()
    scoreboard = []
    for st, grp_label in STATUS_GROUPS:
        glyph, color = STATUS_VISUAL[st]
        n = counts[st]
        scoreboard.append(t.c(color if n else "cinza", f"{glyph} {n} {grp_label}"))
    print("  " + "   ".join(scoreboard))
    frac = done_count / total if total else 0
    print(f"  {t.bar(frac, n=min(40, max(w - 40, 10)))}  "
          + t.c("negrito", f"{round(frac * 100)}%")
          + t.c("cinza", f" fechados ({counts['done']} concluídos + "
                f"{counts['dropped']} descartados) ÷ {total}"))
    for text in owner_lines(lines, program):
        wrapped = t.wrap(text, 4, 4)
        print("  " + t.c("amarelo", "⚑ ") + t.c("amarelo", wrapped[0][4:]))
        for x in wrapped[1:]:
            print(t.c("amarelo", x))
    for st, grp_label in STATUS_GROUPS:
        group = [l for l in visible if l["status"] == st]
        if not group:
            continue
        glyph, color = STATUS_VISUAL[st]
        print()
        print(t.section(grp_label, len(group), color=color, glyph=glyph))
        is_closed = st in ("done", "dropped")
        col_width = min(max(len(str(l["id"])) for l in group), 42)
        for i, l in enumerate(group):
            num = t.c("cinza", f"{l['posicao']:>5}  ")
            if is_closed:
                ident = t.cut(str(l["id"]), col_width).ljust(col_width)
                title = t.cut(" ".join(str(l["title"] or "").split()),
                                 max(w - 9 - col_width, 10))
                print(num + t.c(color, ident) + "  " + t.c("cinza", title))
                if code_line(l["codigo"]):
                    for x in t.wrap("↳ " + code_line(l["codigo"]), 7, 9):
                        print(t.c("vermelho", x))
                continue
            if i:
                print()
            print(num + t.c(f"negrito+{color}", l["id"]))
            for x in t.wrap(" ".join(str(l["title"] or "").split()), 7):
                print(x)
            details = []
            if l["pronto"]:
                details.append(("pronto", "o próximo cepa-until pega", "verde"))
            if l["sem_epic"]:
                details.append(("sem Epic", SEM_EPIC_LINE.split(": ", 1)[1], "amarelo"))
            if l["pegavel"] and not l["pronto"]:
                details.append(("pegável", PEGAVEL_LINE.split(": ", 1)[1], "amarelo"))
            if code_line(l["codigo"]):
                details.append(("código", code_line(l["codigo"]).split("código ", 1)[1],
                                "vermelho"))
            if l["claimed_by"]:
                c = l["claimed_by"]
                details.append(("reservado", f"sessão {c['session_id'] or '?'}"
                                 f" desde {c['started_at'] or '?'}", "ciano"))
            if l["blocked_by"]:
                details.append(("espera", ", ".join(map(str, l["blocked_by"])),
                                 "amarelo"))
            if l["human_pending"] is not None:
                details.append(("ação humana", first_sentence(l["human_pending"]),
                                 "amarelo"))
            if st == "blocked" and blocked_reason(l):
                details.append(("motivo", blocked_reason(l), "vermelho"))
            for label, text, d_color in details:
                key = f"↳ {label}: "
                wrapped = t.wrap(key + text, 7, 7 + len(key))
                print(" " * 7 + t.c(d_color, key) + wrapped[0][7 + len(key):])
                for x in wrapped[1:]:
                    print(x)
    return 0


def cmd_show(root, name, as_json, item_id=None):
    """The queue header: where it came from and what it demonstrates when it ends.

    `status` answers "where do the items stand"; this one answers "what is this
    queue for", which is the question of whoever opens a cycle queue. With an
    item id, the same question about ONE item: `show <fila> <id>`.
    """
    if item_id is not None:
        return cmd_status(root, name, None, as_json, item_id, via_show=True)
    target = queue_path(root, name)
    if not target.is_file():
        print(f"{target} não existe — quem escreve a fila é o /common:queue",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    plan, error = read_plan(target)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if mode_of(plan) != MODE:
        print(f"COLISÃO: {target} é um plano '{mode_of(plan)}' — ondas do "
              "/maestro:program-plan, não uma fila", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    items = plan.get("items") or []
    demonstrates = _read_demonstrates(plan)
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"program": qp.queue_name_of(plan, name),
                          "queue": qp.queue_name_of(plan, name),
                          "path": str(target), "source": plan.get("source"),
                          "demonstrates": demonstrates, "total": len(items)},
                         ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
        return 0
    print(f"fila {qp.queue_name_of(plan, name)} · {target}")
    print(f"  fonte: {plan.get('source') or '(sem `source`)'}")
    print(f"  demonstrates: {demonstrates}" if demonstrates else
          "  sem `demonstrates:` — a fila não diz o que demonstra quando acaba")
    print(f"  {len(items)} itens · a situação de cada um: cepa-plan status {name}"
          f" · um deles em detalhe: cepa-plan show {name} <id>")
    return 0


# ── promotion: the demands the queue hands to /maestro:program-plan ──────────

# Maestro's D7 floor (common/plan-schema.yaml, "Piso de uso"): below 4 demands
# the cost of forking a worktree, bringing up the gatekeeper and landing a
# merge train loses to executing the same queue in series. The floor is checked
# HERE, and not in the command's prose, because command prose erodes without any
# test turning red — the lesson the completeness auditor left on steps 1 and 2.
DEMAND_FLOOR = 4

# Why an item does not become a slice. Each reason is a different loss if the
# promoter stays quiet about it.
OUT_OF_PROMOTION = {
    "done": "já fechou — a fila guarda a evidência, não há trabalho a forkar",
    "dropped": "descartado da fila; o `why` fica no documento, o trabalho não",
    "in_progress": ("reservado por outra sessão (`cepa-plan start`) — forkar "
                    "uma onda por cima duplica o trabalho de quem está nele"),
    "blocked": ("saiu `blocked` de um run anterior, numa condição de fora que "
                "ninguém mexeu desde então; forkar mede o mesmo travamento"),
}


# ── "where are we" of the Epics, derived (read-only) ─────────────────────────

RE_EPIC_QUEUE_PREFIX = re.compile(
    r"([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*)-c(?:<N>|\d+)")
OPEN_STATUSES = ("blocked", "pending", "in_progress")


def epic_cycles(text):
    """[(number, label)] of the Epic's ladder, in table order. The number is the
    leading integer of the "Cycle" cell (`1. Encadear` -> 1, `Encadear`); with
    no integer it is the row position."""
    idx, rows, _ = ladder_rows(text)
    if "ciclo" not in idx:
        return []
    out = []
    for pos, cells in enumerate(rows, 1):
        cell = cells[idx["ciclo"]] if idx["ciclo"] < len(cells) else ""
        cell = " ".join(cell.replace("**", "").split())
        m = re.match(r"(\d+)\s*[.):\-]?\s*(.*)$", cell)
        out.append((int(m.group(1)), m.group(2) or str(m.group(1))) if m
                   else (pos, cell or str(pos)))
    return out


def queue_belongs(slug, epic_rel, header, prefixes, number, qname, plan):
    """Does the single-track queue `qname` belong to cycle `number` of the Epic
    `slug`? True when ANY of the three rules holds:

    (a) the queue `source` contains the Epic path (`docs/epics/<slug>.md`) AND
        mentions `ciclo N` or `cycle N` (what `--from-epic` writes);
    (b) the queue name is `<slug>-c<N>`;
    (c) the Epic HEADER (text before the first `## `) names a queue pattern
        `<prefix>-c<N>` (placeholder) or `<prefix>-c<digits>`, and the queue
        name is `<prefix>-c<N>` (the Epic written by hand, before
        /common:epic, declares its queues this way).
    """
    source = str(plan.get("source") or "")
    if epic_rel in source and re.search(
            rf"\b(?:ciclo|cycle)\s*{number}\b", source, re.I):
        return True
    if qname == f"{slug}-c{number}":
        return True
    return any(qname == f"{pre}-c{number}" for pre in prefixes)


def queue_summary(qname, plan):
    items = [i for i in (plan.get("items") or []) if isinstance(i, dict)]
    counts = {st: 0 for st in STATUSES}
    for it in items:
        st = status_of(it)
        counts[st] = counts.get(st, 0) + 1
    opened = []
    for it in items:
        st = status_of(it)
        if st in OPEN_STATUSES and (it.get("human_pending")
                                    or it.get("owner_question")):
            opened.append({"id": it.get("id"), "status": st,
                           "human_pending": it.get("human_pending") or None,
                           "question": it.get("owner_question") or None})
    return {"queue": qname, "counts": counts,
            "in_progress": [it.get("id") for it in items
                            if status_of(it) == "in_progress"],
            "open": opened}


def queue_closed(summary):
    """Closed = at least one `done` and nothing else but `done`/`dropped`. An
    empty queue (`items: []`) is therefore NOT closed: it stays `em-andamento`
    with 0/0, because nothing was ever delivered."""
    c = summary["counts"]
    return c.get("done", 0) > 0 and (
        c.get("done", 0) + c.get("dropped", 0) == sum(c.values()))


def epic_report(root, path, queues):
    """One Epic's report. `queues` is {name: plan} of the single-track queues."""
    text = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    slug = path.stem
    rel = f"docs/epics/{path.name}"
    m = re.search(r"^#\s+Epic:\s*(.+?)\s*$", text, re.M)
    st = re.search(r"^\*\*Status:\*\*\s*([^\s·*]+)", text, re.M)
    first = RE_SECTION.search(text)
    header = text[:first.start()] if first else text
    prefixes = sorted(set(RE_EPIC_QUEUE_PREFIX.findall(header)))
    cycles, missing = [], []
    for number, label in epic_cycles(text):
        linked = [queue_summary(n, pl) for n, pl in sorted(queues.items())
                  if queue_belongs(slug, rel, header, prefixes, number, n, pl)]
        if not linked:
            state = "sem-fila"
            missing.append(f"ciclo {number} {label} sem fila")
        elif all(queue_closed(x) for x in linked):
            state = "fechado"
        else:
            state = "em-andamento"
            pend = sum(x["counts"].get("pending", 0) for x in linked)
            blk = sum(x["counts"].get("blocked", 0) for x in linked)
            missing.append(f"ciclo {number} {label}: {pend} pending, "
                           f"{blk} blocked")
        cycles.append({"number": number, "label": label, "state": state,
                       "queues": linked})
    questions = [first_sentence(mm.group(1), 200) for mm in
                 re.finditer(r"^\s*-\s+\[ \]\s*(.*)$", text, re.M)]
    return {"name": slug, "path": rel,
            "queue_prefix": prefixes[0] if prefixes else None,
            "title": m.group(1) if m else None,
            "status": st.group(1) if st else None,
            "cycles": cycles, "open_questions": questions,
            "missing": missing}


def _tally(cycle):
    done = sum(x["counts"].get("done", 0) for x in cycle["queues"])
    total = sum(sum(x["counts"].values()) for x in cycle["queues"])
    return done, total


def _runs(numbers):
    """[2,3,4,6] -> "2-4, 6"."""
    parts, i = [], 0
    while i < len(numbers):
        j = i
        while j + 1 < len(numbers) and numbers[j + 1] == numbers[j] + 1:
            j += 1
        parts.append(str(numbers[i]) if i == j
                     else f"{numbers[i]}-{numbers[j]}")
        i = j + 1
    return ", ".join(parts)


def epic_text(e):
    lines = [f"Epic {e['name']} (Status: {e['status'] or '?'}) · {e['path']}"]
    for c in e["cycles"]:
        done, total = _tally(c)
        head = f"  ciclo {c['number']} {c['label']}: "
        names = ", ".join(x["queue"] for x in c["queues"])
        if c["state"] == "sem-fila":
            lines.append(head + "sem fila")
        elif c["state"] == "fechado":
            lines.append(head + f"fechado — fila {names}, {done}/{total} done")
        else:
            sums = {st: sum(x["counts"].get(st, 0) for x in c["queues"])
                    for st in STATUSES}
            extra = "".join(f", {sums[st]} {st}" for st in
                            ("pending", "in_progress", "blocked") if sums[st])
            lines.append(head + f"em andamento — fila {names}, "
                         f"{done}/{total} done{extra}")
    qs = e["open_questions"]
    if qs:
        lines.append(f"  pendente com o dono: {len(qs)} pergunta(s) em "
                     "aberto no Epic")
        lines += [f"    - {q}" for q in qs]
    for c in e["cycles"]:
        for x in c["queues"]:
            for o in x["open"]:
                what = (f'pergunta: "{o["question"]}"' if o["question"]
                        else f'pendente: "{o["human_pending"]}"')
                lines.append(f"  fila em andamento: {o['id']} ({x['queue']}) "
                             f"{o['status']} — {what}")
    nxt = next((c for c in e["cycles"] if c["state"] == "sem-fila"), None)
    if nxt:
        lines.append(f"  próximo ciclo sem fila: {nxt['number']} "
                     f"{nxt['label']} → /common:queue "
                     f"{e.get('queue_prefix') or e['name']}-c"
                     f"{nxt['number']} --from-epic {e['path']} --cycle "
                     f"{nxt['number']}")
    return "\n".join(lines)


def epic_brief(e, limit=200):
    def body(labels):
        parts = []
        for c in e["cycles"]:
            if c["state"] == "sem-fila":
                continue
            done, total = _tally(c)
            name = f"ciclo {c['number']}" + (f" {c['label']}" if labels else "")
            parts.append(f"{name} " + ("fechado" if c["state"] == "fechado"
                                       else "em andamento")
                         + f" ({done}/{total})")
        free = [c["number"] for c in e["cycles"] if c["state"] == "sem-fila"]
        if free:
            parts.append(f"ciclo{'s' if len(free) > 1 else ''} "
                         f"{_runs(free)} sem fila")
        for c in e["cycles"]:
            for x in c["queues"]:
                if x["open"] and c["state"] == "em-andamento":
                    k = len(x["open"])
                    parts.append(f"{k} pergunta{'s' if k > 1 else ''} "
                                 f"pendente{'s' if k > 1 else ''} na fila "
                                 f"{x['queue']}")
        k = len(e["open_questions"])
        if k:
            parts.append(f"{k} pergunta{'s' if k > 1 else ''} em aberto do dono")
        return "; ".join(parts) or "sem ciclos na escada"

    tail = " Detalhe: /common:whereami."
    line = f"[epic] {e['name']}: {body(True)}.{tail}"
    if len(line) > limit:
        line = f"[epic] {e['name']}: {body(False)}.{tail}"
    if len(line) > limit:
        room = limit - len(tail) - len(f"[epic] {e['name']}: ") - 1
        line = (f"[epic] {e['name']}: {body(False)[:max(room, 0)].rstrip()}…"
                f".{tail}")
    return line


def cmd_epics(root, as_json, brief):
    """Read-only. The "where are we" of each `docs/epics/*.md`, derived from its
    ladder plus the single-track queues linked to each cycle (rules in
    `queue_belongs`). Nothing is written; no Epic -> prints nothing, rc 0."""
    files = sorted((root / "docs" / "epics").glob("*.md")) \
        if (root / "docs" / "epics").is_dir() else []
    queues = {}
    if files:
        for name, qfile in qp.queue_files(root):
            plan, error = read_plan(qfile)
            if error:
                print(f"{error}; o ciclo dessa fila pode aparecer como "
                      "\"sem fila\" por isso", file=sys.stderr)
                continue
            if isinstance(plan, dict) and mode_of(plan) == MODE:
                queues[name] = plan
    reports = []
    for f in files:
        try:
            reports.append(epic_report(root, f, queues))
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) as e:
            print(f"{f}: ilegível ({e.__class__.__name__})", file=sys.stderr)
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"epics": reports}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
    elif brief:
        for e in reports:
            print(epic_brief(e))
    elif reports:
        print("\n\n".join(epic_text(e) for e in reports))
    return 0


def _human_gate(it):
    """An open `human_pending` becomes an OPEN gate in the slice, not silence.

    The field exists so the debt to the human does not vanish. An item promoted
    with the route open and no gate would fork a child to build on top of
    something nobody validated — and `cepa-dor` (intake) is precisely what
    refuses `open:`, so declaring it is what makes the mechanical gate see it.
    """
    route = it.get("human_pending")
    if isinstance(route, str) and route.strip():
        return "open: " + " ".join(route.split())
    return "none"


def queue_demands(items):
    """(demands, excluded, warnings) — who can become a slice, who cannot, and why.

    Queue ORDER is preserved: this function never reorders. What it adds is
    `onda_minima`, the wave floor that `blocked_by` imposes — two items of the
    same promotion where one depends on the other CANNOT fork together, and
    grouping by disjoint surface without looking at the dependency is the error
    the waves plan pays for with a whole wave redone.

    A `done` blocker does not count (already closed). A `dropped` blocker also
    leaves the field, but WARNED: without that the item would stay stuck forever
    on something nobody will close. A blocker that stays open and outside the
    promotion (reserved, stuck, or an id that does not exist in the queue) takes
    the item out too — and in cascade, because whoever depended on it also
    loses footing.
    """
    warnings = []
    candidates, excluded = [], []
    by_id = {}
    for it in items:
        if not isinstance(it, dict):
            continue
        ident = str(it.get("id"))
        by_id[ident] = it
        st = status_of(it)
        if st == "pending":
            candidates.append(it)
        else:
            excluded.append({"id": ident, "status": st,
                         "motivo": OUT_OF_PROMOTION.get(st, f"status {st!r}")})

    closed = {i for i, it in by_id.items() if status_of(it) == "done"}
    dropped_ids = {i for i, it in by_id.items() if status_of(it) == "dropped"}

    # Cascade: removing a candidate may remove whoever depended on it. Repeats
    # until the set stops changing — the queue has no cycle (`validate` refuses
    # it), so this terminates.
    alive = {str(it.get("id")) for it in candidates}
    deps = {}
    while True:
        changed = False
        for it in candidates:
            ident = str(it.get("id"))
            if ident not in alive:
                continue
            mine = []
            for b in (it.get("blocked_by") or []):
                b = str(b)
                if b in closed:
                    continue
                if b in dropped_ids:
                    # The cascade runs the list more than once; the warning is
                    # about the PAIR (item, blocker), not about the pass.
                    warning = (f"{ident} depende de {b}, que está `dropped` na "
                             "fila — a dependência saiu do campo; se ela ainda "
                             "valer, o item não é candidato a onda")
                    if warning not in warnings:
                        warnings.append(warning)
                    continue
                if b in alive:
                    mine.append(b)
                    continue
                st = status_of(by_id[b]) if b in by_id else "inexistente"
                excluded.append({"id": ident, "status": "pending",
                             "motivo": f"depende de {b} ({st}), que não entra "
                                       "nesta promoção — a onda forkaria sobre "
                                       "um pé que ninguém vai fechar"})
                alive.discard(ident)
                changed = True
                break
            else:
                deps[ident] = mine
        if not changed:
            break

    ordered = [it for it in candidates if str(it.get("id")) in alive]

    # `onda_minima` by fixed point: 1 for whoever depends on no one in the
    # promotion, 1 + the largest floor of the blockers for the rest. Fixed point,
    # and not a single pass, because `blocked_by` may point to an item that comes
    # AFTER in the queue (the order is of execution, not topological).
    floor = {str(it.get("id")): 1 for it in ordered}
    for _ in range(len(ordered) + 1):
        stable = True
        for ident, mine in deps.items():
            if ident not in floor:
                continue
            target = max([1] + [floor[b] + 1 for b in mine if b in floor])
            if target != floor[ident]:
                floor[ident] = target
                stable = False
        if stable:
            break

    demands = []
    for it in ordered:
        ident = str(it.get("id"))
        demands.append({
            "id": ident,
            "title": it.get("title"),
            "why": it.get("why"),
            "depends_on": deps.get(ident, []),
            "onda_minima": floor[ident],
            "human_gate": _human_gate(it),
        })
    return demands, excluded, warnings


def queue_source(plan, name, target, promoted, total, when):
    """The `source:` line of the waves plan — trace back to the queue.

    Without it the waves plan is born orphaned: nobody can say, months later,
    which queue that slice came from nor what state it was in. Each slice's
    `demanda` is the item's `id`, and this line is the other end of the thread.
    """
    text = (f"fila single-track '{name}' ({target}) — {promoted} de {total} "
             f"itens promovidos a slice por /maestro:program-plan --from-plan")
    if when:
        text += f", em {when}"
    origin = plan.get("source")
    if origin:
        text += f" · a fila veio de: {origin}"
    return text


def cmd_promote(root, name, as_json, when):
    target = queue_path(root, name)
    if not target.is_file():
        print(f"{target} não existe — não há fila para promover. Quem escreve é "
              "o /common:queue.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    plan, error = read_plan(target)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if mode_of(plan) != MODE:
        print(f"{target} já é um plano '{mode_of(plan)}' — ondas não se promovem "
              "a ondas. Quem executa esse documento é o /maestro:run.",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    gaps = validate_plan(plan)
    if gaps:
        print(f"{target}: {len(gaps)} lacuna(s) — não dá para promover uma fila "
              "inválida", file=sys.stderr)
        for f in gaps:
            print(f"  - {f}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    items = plan.get("items") or []
    demands, excluded, warnings = queue_demands(items)
    waves = max([d["onda_minima"] for d in demands], default=0)
    floor_ok = len(demands) >= DEMAND_FLOOR
    output = {
        "program": qp.queue_name_of(plan, name),
        "queue": qp.queue_name_of(plan, name),
        "path": str(target),
        "source": queue_source(plan, name, target, len(demands), len(items), when),
        "demands": demands,
        "excluded": excluded,
        "warnings": warnings,
        "floor": {"minimo": DEMAND_FLOOR, "demandas": len(demands),
                  "atingido": floor_ok},
        "ondas_minimas": waves,
    }
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(output, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
    else:
        print(f"fila {output['queue']} · {target}")
        for d in demands:
            dep = f" (depois de {', '.join(d['depends_on'])})" if d["depends_on"] else ""
            print(f"  onda ≥{d['onda_minima']}  {d['id']} — {d['title']}{dep}")
            if d["human_gate"] != "none":
                print(f"     gate humano ABERTO: {d['human_gate'][6:]}")
        for f in excluded:
            print(f"  fora: {f['id']} ({f['status']}) — {f['motivo']}")
        for a in warnings:
            print(f"  aviso: {a}")
        print(f"  {len(demands)} demanda(s) · piso D7 = {DEMAND_FLOOR} · "
              f"{waves} onda(s) no mínimo pela dependência")

    if not floor_ok:
        detail = ("a fila não tem nenhum item `pending` para promover"
                   if not demands else
                   f"só {len(demands)} demanda(s) — o piso D7 é {DEMAND_FLOOR}")
        print(f"PISO NÃO ATINGIDO: {detail}. Abaixo dele o fork perde para "
              "executar a mesma fila em série: /common:drain-plan "
              f"{name}.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 4
    return 0


# ── marking: the batch reserves the item before and records the outcome after ─

def file_header(text):
    """The top comments, verbatim.

    Rewriting the whole file through `serialize` would regenerate the header
    from a `--when` that the marking does not have — and dating the document
    with TODAY's date every time an item closes erases when the queue was
    written.
    """
    lines = []
    for line in text.splitlines(keepends=True):
        if line.startswith("#") or not line.strip():
            lines.append(line)
        else:
            break
    return "".join(lines)


def write_body(target, plan, items):
    body = dict(plan)
    body["items"] = items
    dump = yaml.dump(body, allow_unicode=True, sort_keys=False,
                     default_flow_style=False, width=78)
    text = file_header(target.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    if text and not text.endswith("\n\n"):
        text += "\n"
    tmp = target.with_suffix(".yaml.tmp")
    tmp.write_text(text + dump, encoding="utf-8")
    tmp.replace(target)


# ── after writing: commit or warning ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Every write used to leave plan.yaml modified and silent. On 2026-10-15 the
# owner ran `answer` three times and each time the queue was left uncommitted:
# an agent committed afterwards, one of the answers went into someone else's
# commit with the wrong message, and `cepa-until`, which refuses a dirty tree,
# did not start (fb-20261015-1).
# Rule: the owner's door (`answer`, `add`) commits the queue in the same step,
# only it (`git commit -- <path>`), and `--no-commit` turns it off; marking a
# batch (`start`, `finish`) warns that a commit is missing and `--commit` turns
# it on — inside a `cepa-until` run the clone stays modified on purpose until
# the owner returns, and a commit per item would be one commit per item on the
# branch the owner has open in the clone. The exit never changes because of
# this: the write happened.

def _git(root, *args):
    try:
        p = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(root), *args],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        return 1, "", str(e)
    return p.returncode, p.stdout, p.stderr


def _queue_rel(root, target):
    try:
        return str(Path(target).resolve().relative_to(Path(root).resolve()))
    except ValueError:
        return str(target)


def other_changes(root, rel):
    """The `git status` lines that are NOT the queue (None if git failed)."""
    rc, out, _ = _git(root, "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=no")
    if rc != 0:
        return None
    return [l for l in out.splitlines() if l.strip() and rel not in l]


def close_write(root, target, message, commit, inside_run=None, extras=()):
    """Called after `write_body`: commits only the queue, or says that one is missing.

    `extras`: other paths the same write touched (the waivers of `answer`).
    They enter the commit only if `git add` accepts them; `.claude/` is
    ignored in host repos and `add` refuses — then the file stays out,
    without failing the write.

    The queue itself is added with `-f`. Host repos ignore `.claude/` whole
    (WEGO's `.gitignore` line 79), so a plain `add` refused `plan.yaml` on
    every write, the warning came back on every answer, and the command it
    suggested failed the same way: the queue of WEGO had no version at all
    (fb-20261103-1). The queue is Cepa's own file and the owner decided it is
    versioned, ignored directory or not."""
    rel = _queue_rel(root, target)
    q = shlex.quote(str(root))
    command = (f"git -C {q} add -f -- {rel} && "
               f"git -C {q} commit -m {shlex.quote(message)} -- {rel}")
    if commit:
        rc, _, err = _git(root, "add", "-f", "--", rel)
        included = [rel]
        if rc == 0:
            for extra in extras:
                if _git(root, "add", "--", _queue_rel(root, extra))[0] == 0:
                    included.append(_queue_rel(root, extra))
            rc, _, err = _git(root, "commit", "-q", "-m", message, "--", *included)
        if rc == 0:
            _, sha, _ = _git(root, "rev-parse", "--short", "HEAD")
            print(f"  commit {sha.strip()}: {message} ({rel})")
            others = other_changes(root, rel)
            if others:
                print(f"  aviso: o clone tem {len(others)} outra(s) mudança(s) "
                      "sem commit; o commit levou só a fila")
            return True
        reason = [l for l in (err or "").strip().splitlines() if l.strip()]
        print(f"  aviso: a fila foi gravada mas NÃO commitada "
              f"({reason[-1] if reason else 'o git falhou'}). Falta commitar: "
              f"{command}")
        return False
    if inside_run is None:
        inside_run = bool(os.environ.get("CEPA_UNTIL_RUN"))
    if inside_run:
        print(f"  fila gravada sem commit ({rel}): dentro de um run do "
              "cepa-until o clone fica assim de propósito; o dono commita "
              "a fila depois do run")
    else:
        print(f"  fila gravada sem commit ({rel}). Falta commitar: {command} "
              "— ou passe --commit para gravar e commitar no mesmo passo")
    return False


def open_plan_for_marking(root, name):
    """(target, plan, item_by_id, exit_error) — the common read of start/finish."""
    target = queue_path(root, name)
    if not target.is_file():
        print(f"{target} não existe — não há fila para marcar", file=sys.stderr)
        return None, None, None, 2
    plan, error = read_plan(target)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return None, None, None, 2
    if mode_of(plan) != MODE:
        print(f"{target} é um plano '{mode_of(plan)}', não uma fila", file=sys.stderr)
        return None, None, None, 3
    return target, plan, {str(i.get("id")): i for i in (plan.get("items") or [])
                        if isinstance(i, dict)}, 0


def cmd_start(root, name, ident, cwd=".", commit=False):
    target, plan, by_id, rc = open_plan_for_marking(root, name)
    if rc:
        return rc
    it = by_id.get(str(ident))
    if it is None:
        print(f"a fila {name} não tem item '{ident}' — os que ela tem: "
              + ", ".join(by_id) or "(nenhum)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    st = status_of(it)
    recovered = ""
    if st == "in_progress":
        # The reservation now has an owner, so the refusal stops being generic:
        # with a live owner it NAMES who is on the item; with a dead owner, the
        # reservation is orphaned and claiming it is right — the alternative was
        # the queue jamming forever because of a run that ended.
        state, detail = reservation_of(it, root)
        if state != "orfa":
            print(f"{ident} JÁ está `in_progress`: {detail}. Executar por cima "
                  "refaz trabalho; a reserva é o que impede isso.",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 5
        recovered = f"  reserva órfã recuperada: {detail}"
    elif st != "pending":
        print(f"{ident} está `{st}`, não `pending` — o lote só reserva item "
              "pendente", file=sys.stderr)
        return 5
    if it.get("human_pending") is not None:
        print(f"{ident} tem uma rota aberta que só você fecha "
              f"({it['human_pending']}) — o lote não passa por cima dela",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 5
    it["status"] = "in_progress"
    # The resolved TREE ROOT on purpose: `finish` compares this `cwd` with the
    # caller's tree (DUR-2), a "." stored here would match every tree, and a
    # `finish` run from a subdirectory must still match the owner.
    it["claimed_by"] = current_owner(root, session_root(cwd))
    write_body(target, plan, plan.get("items") or [])
    print(f"{ident} reservado (`in_progress`) em {target}")
    if recovered:
        print(recovered)
    owner = it["claimed_by"]
    print(f"  dono: {owner['session_id']} (host {owner['hostname']}, "
          f"pid {owner['pid']}) — é o que responde \"outra sessão está nele "
          "agora ou um run morreu?\" no próximo `queue`")
    # The note from whoever took the item out of here before (`cepa-until` returns
    # the red-build item to `pending`, with the lateral and the reason): the
    # reader is the agent that just reserved. Without printing, nobody read it.
    previous = str(it.get("evidence") or "").strip()
    if previous:
        print("  evidence anterior (leia antes de começar):")
        for line in previous.splitlines():
            print(f"    {line}")
    close_write(root, target, f"queue {name}: start {ident}", commit)
    return 0


def session_root(repo):
    """The root of `repo`'s worktree (`_wtlib.session_root`), not the main clone
    where the queue lives: build, topology and gate artifacts follow the tree
    where the item was built."""
    w = _wt()
    if w:
        return Path(w.session_root(repo))
    r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(repo), "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"],
                       capture_output=True, text=True)
    return Path(r.stdout.strip() if r.returncode == 0 else repo)


def empty_build(repo):
    """The `.claude/last-build.json` at the root of `repo`'s SESSION, if it is EMPTY
    (or STALE whose last real run was EMPTY).

    The build baseline follows the worktree (`_wtlib.session_root`), not the
    main clone where the queue lives. EMPTY is a test filter that came out green
    without executing any test (recorded by capture-build-result); absent or
    unreadable returns None — green or red is gate-advance's business.
    """
    p = session_root(repo) / ".claude" / "last-build.json"
    try:
        state = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    if not isinstance(state, dict):
        return None
    status = str(state.get("status", "")).upper()
    if status == "EMPTY":
        state["_arquivo"] = str(p)
        return state
    # EMPTY followed by a source edit (mark-build-stale → STALE with
    # `last_known_status: EMPTY`): no new build ran since the empty one.
    if status == "STALE" and str(state.get("last_known_status", "")).upper() == "EMPTY":
        return dict(state, _arquivo=str(p), _stale=True,
                    command=state.get("last_known_command"))
    return None


# Topologies whose plan-build-validate ends at the `validation-lead` (security
# review + full build + verdict). Item `drain-plan-pula-validacao-
# build-hex` (2026-09-24): in the 09/23 cepa-until run at WEGO none of the 5
# delivered cards went through it, and WEGO-2318, which logs into the portal with
# the operator's credential, closed `done` without a security review. The test
# test_common_drain_plan checks this list against the repo's
# `agents/validation-lead.md`, so the two do not diverge.
TOPOLOGIES_WITH_VALIDATION = ("build-hex", "build-team")
SHIP_VERDICTS = ("READY-TO-SHIP", "READY-WITH-CAVEATS")
VERDICT_RE = re.compile(r"^verdict:\s*[\"']?([A-Za-z_-]+)", re.MULTILINE)


def missing_validation(repo, ident):
    """None when the item may close `done`; otherwise, the refusal sentence.

    Only applies to a topology with `validation-lead`. The artifact is what
    validation-lead itself writes, `docs/validation/<id>.yaml`, at the session
    root.

    The destination was `.claude/validation/` until 2026-09-27. In projects that
    run the gate `.claude/*` is ignored by git, so the verdict died with the
    run's disposable worktree (the 3 from WEGO's run 2026-09-27-0832 only
    existed in its worktree) — the same reason that moved proof-reviewer to
    `docs/proof/`. The old path is still READ, like proof's: narrowing the
    reader would blind it to the verdicts already on disk.
    """
    sess_root = session_root(repo)
    try:
        topology = (sess_root / ".claude" / "topology").read_text(
            encoding="utf-8").strip()
    except OSError:
        return None
    if topology not in TOPOLOGIES_WITH_VALIDATION:
        return None
    p = sess_root / "docs" / "validation" / f"{ident}.yaml"
    legacy = sess_root / ".claude" / "validation" / f"{ident}.yaml"
    if not p.exists() and legacy.exists():
        p = legacy
    try:
        text = p.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except OSError:
        return (f"a topologia `{topology}` termina no `validation-lead`, e não "
                f"há veredito dele para {ident} ({p} não existe). Sem ele o item "
                "fecha sem a revisão de segurança. Delegue ao validation-lead, "
                "que grava o arquivo; `blocked`/`pending` continuam aceitos.")
    m = VERDICT_RE.search(text)
    verdict = m.group(1).upper() if m else None
    if verdict in SHIP_VERDICTS:
        return None
    return (f"o veredito do `validation-lead` para {ident} é "
            f"`{verdict or '<ausente>'}` ({p}), e só "
            f"{' ou '.join(SHIP_VERDICTS)} fecha `done`. Resolva o que "
            "ele nomeou, ou feche como `blocked` com o motivo.")


# ── validation owed: built, not validated, session ending ───────────────────
#
# On 2026-11-02 a session built WEGO-2416 and WEGO-2012, recorded the evidence,
# left both `pending` because `done` needs the validation-lead verdict, and
# ended its turn asking the owner whether to run the validator
# (fb-20261103-1). The gate held; the session just stopped short of it. Here
# `finish` leaves a marker per item it could not close for lack of that
# verdict, under the session's own folder, and the Stop hook
# `validation-owed-gate.py` refuses to end the turn while one is open.
# `done` or `blocked` on the item clears it, from any session.

def owed_root():
    return Path(os.environ.get("HOME", str(Path.home()))) / ".claude" / "cepa-validation-owed"


def _owed_name(name, ident):
    return re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]", "_", f"{name}__{ident}") + ".json"


def mark_validation_owed(name, ident, repo, gap):
    sid = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID") or os.environ.get("CLAUDE_SESSION_ID")
    if not sid:
        return None
    folder = owed_root() / re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]", "_", sid)
    try:
        folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        path = folder / _owed_name(name, ident)
        path.write_text(json.dumps({"queue": name, "item": str(ident),
                                    "repo": str(Path(repo).resolve()),
                                    "gap": gap, "at": now_iso()},
                                   ensure_ascii=False), encoding="utf-8")
        return path
    except OSError:
        return None


def clear_validation_owed(name, ident):
    for path in owed_root().glob(f"*/{_owed_name(name, ident)}"):
        try:
            path.unlink()
        except OSError:
            pass


def blocked_reason(line):
    """Why a `blocked` item stopped, for a person: the human section's
    `impede` when the agent wrote it, else the first sentence of the agent
    section (items blocked before 2026-11-01)."""
    summary = line.get("owner_summary") or {}
    if isinstance(summary, dict) and summary.get("impede"):
        return " ".join(str(summary["impede"]).split())
    return first_sentence(line["evidence"]) if line.get("evidence") else ""


def human_section_refusal(status, owner, question):
    """Why `finish` refuses the human section, as text, or None.

    `evidence` is for agents and keeps its codes. `owner_summary` and the
    question are for someone who never opened the card, so they carry no
    code at all (see `_ownertext`)."""
    if status == "blocked" and not str(owner.get("impede") or "").strip():
        return ("`blocked` sem `--blocker` (ou `--impede`) não fecha: o dono lê a seção humana "
                "e não o log. Diga, em uma frase leiga, o que impede o item "
                "de andar (ex.: \"o sistema responde em branco quando nega um "
                "acesso, e 18 testes dependem dessa resposta\"). Junte "
                "`--asked` (o que era para fazer) e `--ready` (o que já "
                "funciona). Códigos, commits e vereditos ficam no `--evidence`.")
    bad = []
    for key, flag, _ in _ownertext.FIELDS:
        found = _ownertext.problems(owner.get(key))
        if found:
            bad.append(f"{flag}: {'; '.join(found)}")
    if question is not None:
        found = _ownertext.problems(question, limit=25)
        if found:
            bad.append(f"--question: {'; '.join(found)}")
    if bad:
        return ("a seção humana é lida por quem nunca abriu o card, e estes "
                "campos fogem da regra: " + " | ".join(bad) + ". Reescreva "
                "em palavras leigas. Códigos, commits e vereditos ficam no "
                "`--evidence`, que é a seção dos agentes.")
    return None


# ── finish: who may close the item, and on what commit (DUR-2) ───────────────
#
# 2026-11-05, docs/estrategia-durabilidade.md O1 item 1. `finish` used to
# overwrite `evidence` unconditionally: a second `finish` on an already closed
# item silently erased the first one's evidence (confirmed on disk: two finishes
# leave only the last text), and `done` was accepted with code still uncommitted
# in the tree, which the supervisor then stashed, so the next card never saw it.
# So: a terminal item is not re-marked, only the session that holds the item
# closes it, `done` needs a clean tree and records the HEAD it closed on, and
# every refusal is written on the item (`finish_recusado`) because a refusal
# nobody can read afterwards is the same silence in another place.
# `--supervisor` (cepa-until only) bypasses the first two: the supervisor
# legitimately re-marks what the agent closed (red full build, side branch note).

TERMINAL = ("done", "blocked", "dropped")
NO_SESSION = "sessão não registrada"
KEEP_REFUSALS = 5


def _same_tree(a, b):
    try:
        return os.path.realpath(str(a)) == os.path.realpath(str(b))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return str(a) == str(b)


def _first_line(text):
    for line in str(text or "").splitlines():
        if line.strip():
            return line.strip()
    return ""


def dirty_paths(tree, queue_rel):
    """Paths in `git status` of `tree` that are NOT the queue, its `.yaml.bak`
    or the untracked run records beside it
    (`start` leaves the queue modified inside a `cepa-until` run on purpose).
    None if `tree` is not a git repo."""
    rc, out, _ = _git(tree, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", "HEAD")
    if rc != 0:  # not a repo, or a repo with no commit: there is no SHA to record
        return None
    rc, out, _ = _git(tree, "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=all")
    if rc != 0:
        return None
    queue_dir = os.path.dirname(queue_rel)
    found = []
    for line in out.splitlines():
        if not line.strip():
            continue
        path = line[3:].strip().strip('"')
        if path == queue_rel:
            continue
        # The run's own records (`<queue dir>/until/*`: log, state, heartbeat)
        # are not work; `cepa-until` itself ignores them (RUN_RECORD).
        if line.startswith("??") and path.startswith(queue_dir + "/until/"):
            continue
        if line.startswith("??") and path.endswith(".yaml.bak") \
                and os.path.dirname(path) == queue_dir:
            continue
        found.append(path)
    return found


def finish_gate(root, target, it, ident, status, repo, supervisor):
    """The reason `finish` is refused on this item (rules 1-3 of DUR-2), or None."""
    st = status_of(it)
    if not supervisor and st in TERMINAL:
        first = _first_line(it.get("evidence")) or "(sem evidência)"
        return (f"{ident} já está `{st}`: um segundo `finish` apagaria a "
                f"evidência de quem fechou. Primeira linha dela: \"{first}\"")
    claim = it.get("claimed_by")
    caller = current_owner(root, session_root(repo))
    if not supervisor and isinstance(claim, dict) and claim.get("session_id"):
        if caller.get("session_id") == NO_SESSION:
            same = (caller.get("hostname") == claim.get("hostname")
                    and _same_tree(caller.get("cwd"), claim.get("cwd")))
        else:
            same = caller.get("session_id") == claim.get("session_id")
        if not same:
            return (f"{ident} está reservado por {claim.get('session_id')} "
                    f"(host {claim.get('hostname')}, pid {claim.get('pid')}, "
                    f"cwd {claim.get('cwd')}) e quem chamou foi "
                    f"{caller.get('session_id')} (host {caller.get('hostname')}, "
                    f"pid {caller.get('pid')}, cwd {caller.get('cwd')}). Só o "
                    "dono do item o fecha")
    if status == "done":
        tree = session_root(repo)
        dirty = dirty_paths(tree, _queue_rel(root, target))
        if dirty is None:
            return (f"`done` exige gravar o SHA em que o item fechou, e {tree} "
                    "não é um repositório git com ao menos um commit (ou o git falhou)")
        if dirty:
            shown = ", ".join(dirty[:5]) + (f" e mais {len(dirty) - 5}"
                                            if len(dirty) > 5 else "")
            return (f"`done` exige a árvore limpa e há {len(dirty)} caminho(s) "
                    f"sem commit em {tree}: {shown}. Commite antes de fechar "
                    "(desabilitar ou apagar teste não é conserto)")
    return None


def record_refusal(root, name, target, plan, it, status, reason, commit, repo):
    """Writes the refusal on the item (`finish_recusado`, last 5). Never touches
    status, evidence, claimed_by or the human section."""
    caller = current_owner(root, session_root(repo))
    log = it.get("finish_recusado")
    log = list(log) if isinstance(log, list) else []
    log.append({"quando": now_iso(),
                "quem": {"session_id": caller.get("session_id"),
                         "hostname": caller.get("hostname"),
                         "pid": caller.get("pid")},
                "status_pedido": status,
                "motivo": _first_line(reason)[:300]})
    it["finish_recusado"] = log[-KEEP_REFUSALS:]
    write_body(target, plan, plan.get("items") or [])
    close_write(root, target,
                f"queue {name}: {it.get('id')} finish recusado",
                commit)


def cmd_finish(root, name, ident, status, evidence, human_pending, repo=".",
               question=None, commit=False, owner=None, supervisor=False):
    owner = {k: " ".join(str(v).split()) for k, v in (owner or {}).items()
             if v is not None and str(v).strip()}
    refusal = human_section_refusal(status, owner, question)
    if refusal:
        print(f"`{status}` recusado para {ident}: {refusal}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if status == "done":
        gap = missing_validation(repo, ident)
        if gap is not None:
            mark_validation_owed(name, ident, repo, gap)
            print(f"`done` recusado para {ident}: {gap}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        empty = empty_build(repo)
        if empty is not None:
            changed = (f" E o código mudou depois dele (última edição: "
                     f"{empty.get('after_edit_to', '<desconhecida>')}) sem build "
                     "novo — a baseline é STALE em cima desse EMPTY."
                     if empty.get("_stale") else "")
            print(f"`done` recusado para {ident}: o último build real é EMPTY — o filtro "
                  f"de teste em `{empty.get('command') or '<desconhecido>'}` casou "
                  f"zero teste ({empty['_arquivo']}).{changed} Saiu verde sem rodar teste "
                  "nenhum, então não prova nada. Corrija o nome no filtro "
                  "(-Dtest= / -k / -run / -t) e rode de novo, ou faça o build "
                  "falhar com filtro vazio (Maven: "
                  "-Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=true). Um verde com N > 0 "
                  "testes libera; `blocked`/`pending` continuam aceitos.",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    target, plan, by_id, rc = open_plan_for_marking(root, name)
    if rc:
        return rc
    it = by_id.get(str(ident))
    if it is None:
        print(f"a fila {name} não tem item '{ident}'", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    reason = finish_gate(root, target, it, ident, status, repo, supervisor)
    if reason:
        print(f"`{status}` recusado para {ident}: {reason}", file=sys.stderr)
        record_refusal(root, name, target, plan, it, status, reason, commit, repo)
        return 2
    if not str(evidence or "").strip():
        print(f"desfecho sem evidência não fecha item nenhum: `{status}` é uma "
              "palavra, e o que torna ela auditável é o que aconteceu (commits, "
              "vereditos, o que travou). Todo item `done` desta fila carrega a "
              "dele.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    it["status"] = status
    it["evidence"] = evidence
    it.pop("claimed_by", None)
    if status == "done":
        _, head, _ = _git(session_root(repo), "rev-parse", "HEAD")
        it["head_commit"] = head.strip()
    else:
        it.pop("head_commit", None)  # a re-opened item no longer closes on that commit
    if human_pending is not None:
        if not str(human_pending).strip():
            print("`--human-pending` vazio seria FECHAR a dívida, e só o humano "
                  "fecha: ele é o único que sabe se rodou a rota. Para abrir "
                  "uma, passe o texto dela.", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        it["human_pending"] = human_pending
    if question is not None and str(question).strip():
        it["owner_question"] = " ".join(str(question).split())
    elif status in ("done", "pending"):
        # The question belonged to the jam; the item moved on, and it no longer applies.
        it.pop("owner_question", None)
    if owner:
        it["owner_summary"] = owner
    elif status in ("done", "pending"):
        it.pop("owner_summary", None)
    write_body(target, plan, plan.get("items") or [])
    print(f"{ident} → `{status}` em {target}")
    if status in ("done", "blocked"):
        clear_validation_owed(name, ident)
    elif status == "pending":
        gap = missing_validation(repo, ident)
        if gap is not None and mark_validation_owed(name, ident, repo, gap):
            print(f"  {ident} voltou para `pending` sem o veredito do "
                  "validation-lead. Se ele foi construído, delegue ao "
                  "validation-lead ainda nesta sessão e feche com `done`; o "
                  "fim do turno cobra isso.")
    if human_pending:
        print(f"  rota aberta para você: {human_pending}")
    close_write(root, target, f"queue {name}: {ident} -> {status}", commit)
    return 0


# ── answer: the owner unblocks a deferred item ──────────────────────────────
#
# `finish` never closes a human route, and nobody returned a `blocked` to the
# queue: both waited for the owner to edit plan.yaml by hand, and the end of
# `cepa-until` only said "14 ficaram adiados". `answer` is the owner's door,
# and so it requires a terminal: a run's `claude -p` has no TTY, so an agent
# cannot close the route in the human's place through this path.
#
# `--keep` records the answer without touching status or route. Without it,
# every answer unblocked: on 2026-09-30 the owner answered "mantenha travado" to
# WEGO-2337 and "não liguei" to WEGO-1933, and both went back to `pending`,
# ready for the next run to execute what the owner had said to hold.

# What is NOT an answer. On 2026-10-14 (fb-20261014-4) an "eu nao entendi a
# pergunta" said in chat about ANOTHER matter ended up in the evidence of
# S5-nivel-atendimento as "Resposta do dono", and needed a corrective commit:
# `answer` recorded whatever it received. Now it shows the route's question
# and refuses (exit 6) text that asks for clarification or that is itself a
# question. The answer assembled by `cepa-until decide` starts with
# "sim: " / "não: " followed by the drafted question, and so passes straight
# through: the question there is a quotation, not a doubt. `--force` records
# anyway.
ASKS_FOR_CLARIFICATION = re.compile(
    r"\b(n[aã]o|nem|nunca)\s+(entendi|compreendi|captei|ficou\s+claro|"
    r"sei\s+(o\s+que|do\s+que|qual|a\s+que)|sei\s+responder)\b"
    r"|\bcomo\s+assim\b|\bque\s+pergunta\s+[eé]\s+ess|"
    r"\b(o\s+que|oq)\s+(isso\s+|ela\s+)?(quer\s+dizer|significa)\b|"
    r"\b(repet\w*|refa\w+|explic\w+)\s+(a\s+)?pergunta\b", re.I)
DECIDE_ANSWER = re.compile(r"^(sim|n[aã]o)\s*:", re.I)


def not_an_answer(text):
    """The reason `text` does not answer a route, or None."""
    clean = str(text or "").strip()
    if not re.search(r"\w", clean):
        return "só pontuação, sem palavra nenhuma"
    if DECIDE_ANSWER.match(clean):
        return None
    if ASKS_FOR_CLARIFICATION.search(clean):
        return "o texto pede esclarecimento em vez de responder"
    if clean.endswith("?"):
        return "o texto é uma pergunta, não uma resposta"
    return None


# ── answer × proposed waiver ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# In an autonomous run the agent does NOT write a waiver: it writes a PROPOSAL in
# `.claude/waivers/*.yaml` (`status: proposta`, `autor: null`, `fila`, `item`) and
# opens the human route on the item. Whoever converts it into a waiver is the
# owner's `answer`, in a terminal (fb-20261014-3). The reading/writing below is
# the INLINE TWIN of `convert`/`decline` in board-flow/bin/waivers.py — I do
# not import that module because imports between plugins break with the versioned
# cache directories; the test tests/test_cepa_plan_answer_waiver.py checks that
# the two agree.

def _waiver_dirs(root, repo):
    dirs = [Path(root) / ".claude" / "waivers"]
    local_dir = Path(repo).resolve() / ".claude" / "waivers"
    if local_dir != dirs[0].resolve() and local_dir.is_dir():
        dirs.append(local_dir)
    return dirs


def item_proposals(root, repo, name, ident):
    """[(path, dict)] of the pending proposals tied to this queue item."""
    found = []
    for folder in _waiver_dirs(root, repo):
        for path in sorted(folder.glob("*.yaml")):
            try:
                d = yaml.safe_load(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
            except (yaml.YAMLError, OSError):
                continue
            if (isinstance(d, dict) and d.get("status") == "proposta"
                    and str(d.get("item")) == str(ident)
                    and (not d.get("fila") or d.get("fila") == name)):
                found.append((path, d))
    return found


def owner_author(root, author=None):
    if author and author.strip():
        return author.strip()
    rc, out, _ = _git(root, "config", "user.name")
    if rc == 0 and out.strip():
        return out.strip()
    return os.environ.get("USER", "").strip()


def decide_waivers(proposals, answer, keep, today, author):
    """Applies the answer to the proposals and returns (output_lines, sentences)."""
    output, sentences = [], []
    if not proposals:
        return output, sentences
    if keep:
        output.append(f"  {len(proposals)} dispensa(s) proposta(s) seguem "
                     "pendente(s): --keep não decide dispensa")
        return output, [f"Dispensa {d.get('motivo')} em {d.get('escopo')}: "
                       "segue proposta." for _, d in proposals]
    if re.match(r"^sim\b", answer, re.IGNORECASE):
        for path, d in proposals:
            new = {k: v for k, v in d.items() if k not in ("status", "autor")}
            new["autor"] = author
            new["criado_em"] = today
            new["resposta_do_dono"] = answer
            path.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(new, allow_unicode=True,
                                           sort_keys=False), encoding="utf-8")
            output.append(f"  dispensa aceita pelo dono: {path}")
            sentences.append(f"Dispensa {d.get('motivo')} em {d.get('escopo')}: "
                          "aceita pelo dono.")
    elif re.match(r"^n(ã|a)o\b", answer, re.IGNORECASE):
        for path, d in proposals:
            d.update(status="recusada", recusada_em=today,
                     resposta_do_dono=answer)
            path.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d, allow_unicode=True,
                                           sort_keys=False), encoding="utf-8")
            output.append(f"  dispensa recusada: {path}")
            sentences.append(f"Dispensa {d.get('motivo')} em {d.get('escopo')}: "
                          "recusada pelo dono.")
    else:
        output.append(f"  {len(proposals)} dispensa(s) proposta(s) seguem "
                     "pendente(s): só uma resposta que começa com \"sim\" ou "
                     "\"não\" decide dispensa")
        sentences = [f"Dispensa {d.get('motivo')} em {d.get('escopo')}: segue "
                  "proposta." for _, d in proposals]
    return output, sentences


def cmd_answer(root, name, ident, answer, keep=False, force=False,
                 commit=True, repo=".", author=None, drop=False):
    if not sys.stdin.isatty():
        print("`answer` é a resposta do dono e só roda num terminal: sem "
              "TTY, quem chama é um agente, e só o humano fecha uma rota "
              "`human_pending` ou destrava um `blocked`.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    answer = " ".join(str(answer or "").split())
    if not answer:
        print("resposta vazia não destrava nada: o próximo run precisa saber "
              "o que você decidiu ou viu.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if keep and drop:
        print("--keep e --drop se contradizem: um deixa o item como está, o "
              "outro o tira da fila.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    target, plan, by_id, rc = open_plan_for_marking(root, name)
    if rc:
        return rc
    it = by_id.get(str(ident))
    if it is None:
        print(f"a fila {name} não tem item '{ident}'", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    st = status_of(it)
    route = it.get("human_pending")
    # A plain `pending` the owner gives up on is reachable only with `--drop`
    # (WEGO-2463 on 2026-11-02: "descarto este pedido? sim" sent it back to
    # `pending`, and the next run would have picked it up again).
    if st != "blocked" and route is None and not (drop and st == "pending"):
        print(f"{ident} está `{st}` e sem rota humana aberta: não há o que "
              "responder.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    route_question = it.get("owner_question") or route
    if not force:
        reason = not_an_answer(answer)
        if reason:
            print(f"resposta recusada para {ident}: {reason}; nada foi gravado.",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            if route_question:
                print(f"  a rota pergunta: {route_question}", file=sys.stderr)
            print("  responda a essa pergunta (sim/não e o porquê, numa "
                  "linha). Se o texto é mesmo a sua resposta, repita com "
                  "--force.", file=sys.stderr)
            return 6
    today = datetime.now().strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
    previous = " ".join(str(it.get("evidence") or "").split())
    parts = [f"Resposta do dono em {today}: {answer}."]
    proposals = item_proposals(root, repo, name, ident)
    waiver_lines, waiver_sentences = decide_waivers(
        proposals, answer, keep, today,
        owner_author(root, author) if proposals else None)
    parts.extend(waiver_sentences)
    if keep:
        parts.append(f"O dono manteve o item como estava (`{st}`"
                      + (", rota humana aberta" if route is not None else "")
                      + ").")
    else:
        if route is not None:
            parts.append(f"Rota humana fechada pelo dono: {route}.")
            # Explicit null, not absence: the queue validator (and cepa-until)
            # require the key present — "a chave ausente é omissão, e a dívida
            # com o humano volta a ser invisível" (seen on 2026-10-15: S5's
            # answer erased the key and cepa-until refused the queue).
            it["human_pending"] = None
        if drop and st == "done":
            # A delivered item stays delivered: dropping it means the leftover
            # task no longer applies, not that the work is undone.
            parts.append("O dono deu a tarefa que sobrou como encerrada; o "
                          "item segue `done`.")
        elif drop:
            it["status"] = "dropped"
            parts.append(f"O dono descartou o item (estava `{st}`).")
        elif st == "blocked":
            it["status"] = "pending"
            parts.append("O item voltou de `blocked` para `pending`.")
    if previous:
        parts.append(f"Evidência anterior: {previous}")
    it["evidence"] = " ".join(parts)
    if not keep:
        # Kept, the question stays open and the next `cepa-until decide` redoes it.
        it.pop("owner_question", None)
        it.pop("owner_summary", None)
    it.pop("claimed_by", None)
    write_body(target, plan, plan.get("items") or [])
    if keep:
        print(f"{ident} continua `{st}` em {target} · resposta gravada")
    else:
        print(f"{ident} → `{status_of(it)}` em {target}"
              + (" · rota humana fechada" if route is not None else ""))
    for line in waiver_lines:
        print(line)
    close_write(root, target, f"queue {name}: owner's answer to {ident} "
                  f"({status_of(it)})", commit,
                  extras=[p for p, _ in proposals])
    return 0


# ── add: an entry door appends ONE item without rewriting the queue ─────────
#
# A1 of "Fila única, BACKLOG.md e plan.yaml convergem no plan.yaml" (owner's
# decision, 2026-09-25, rule R2): every entry door — /board-flow:capture,
# `cepa-feedback triage`, or the owner's hand — creates the item in the plan IN
# THE SAME STEP in which the card is born, at the end of the queue with "ainda
# não priorizado" if nobody said where it enters. Unlike `write`, which
# rewrites the whole list and so serves to REPLAN, `add` touches only the new
# item — the others, and the hand-written header, survive intact.

NOT_PRIORITIZED_PHRASE = "ainda não priorizado: entrou no fim da fila"


def cmd_add(root, name, ident, a):
    target, plan, by_id, rc = open_plan_for_marking(root, name)
    if rc == 2:
        print(f"  crie a fila primeiro: /common:queue {name}", file=sys.stderr)
        return rc
    if rc:
        return rc

    if str(ident) in by_id:
        it = by_id[str(ident)]
        print(f"{name} já tem o item '{ident}' (status: {status_of(it)}) — "
              "nada foi gravado", file=sys.stderr)
        return 4

    items = list(plan.get("items") or [])

    pos = len(items)
    if a.before:
        if str(a.before) not in by_id:
            print(f"`--before` aponta para '{a.before}', que não existe "
                  f"na fila {name}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        if not str(a.why or "").strip():
            print("inserir antes de outro item exige `--why`: uma posição "
                  "escolhida sem o motivo de vir antes das outras é "
                  "exatamente o que esta fila existe para impedir", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        why = a.why
        pos = next(i for i, it in enumerate(items)
                   if str(it.get("id")) == str(a.before))
    else:
        why = (f"{a.why.strip()} ({NOT_PRIORITIZED_PHRASE})"
               if str(a.why or "").strip() else NOT_PRIORITIZED_PHRASE)

    blockers = []
    if a.blocked_by:
        blockers = [x.strip() for x in a.blocked_by.split(",") if x.strip()]
        missing = [b for b in blockers if b not in by_id]
        if missing:
            print(f"`--blocked-by` cita {', '.join(missing)}, que não "
                  f"existe(m) na fila {name} — id fantasma deixaria o item "
                  "bloqueado para sempre por algo que ninguém vai fechar",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 2

    new = normalize({"id": ident, "title": a.title, "why": why,
                      "status": "pending", "blocked_by": blockers,
                      "human_pending": None, "evidence": None,
                      "sem_epic": True})
    new_items = list(items)
    new_items.insert(pos, new)

    gaps = validate_plan({**plan, "items": new_items})
    if gaps:
        print(f"{len(gaps)} lacuna(s) no resultado — nada foi gravado",
              file=sys.stderr)
        for f in gaps:
            print(f"  - {f}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    write_body(target, plan, new_items)
    print(f"{ident} inserido na posição {pos + 1} de {len(new_items)} em {target}")
    close_write(root, target, f"queue {name}: add {ident}",
                  not getattr(a, "no_commit", False))
    return 0


# ── subcommands ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── reconcile: the plan against the board, in code ───────────────────────────
#
# Reconciliation used to exist only in the PROSE of /common:next (the "plan says /
# board says" table), which caused two problems at once: a batch had no way to
# reconcile without becoming a second reconciler with the rule rewritten, and
# the rule itself had no test — a `.md` proves the command PROMISES, never that
# an execution kept the promise. Here the comparison is code, and the callers are
# both `/common:next --sync` and `/common:drain-plan` before assembling the batch.
#
# Jira access is NOT here: whoever talks to Jira is `atlassian-expert`, the
# only agent with the tools. The command delegates the read, saves the result in
# a file and passes `--board`. This script compares and writes.

# Role of each board status in the queue's life. The keys are those of
# board-flow.yaml's `defaults.status_map`, whose VALUES are the literal Jira
# names of that team ("Doing", "Code Review"...) — which is why the map is read
# from the file, never guessed.
STATUS_ROLE = {
    "done": "done",
    # In Review is the NORMAL destination of an item that closed here: the card
    # waits for the proof gate. Treating it as in-progress read every `done` in
    # Review as a bounce and reopened finished work (run 2026-09-26-1102: 8 items
    # per round). A real bounce puts the card in in_progress/to_do.
    "in_review": "em-revisao",
    "in_progress": "em-andamento",
    "to_do": "a-fazer",
    "blocked": "a-fazer",
    "wont_do": "descartado",
    "cancelled": "descartado",
}


def repo_status_map(root, config=None):
    """(name-literal → role mapping, path, error). With no board configured, ({}, ...)."""
    candidates = ([Path(config)] if config else
                  [root / "board-flow.yaml",
                   root / ".claude" / "board-flow.lifecycle.yaml"])
    for c in candidates:
        if not c.is_file():
            continue
        try:
            cfg = yaml.safe_load(c.read_text(encoding="utf-8")) or {}
        except (yaml.YAMLError, OSError) as e:
            return {}, str(c), f"{c} está ilegível ({e.__class__.__name__}: {e})"
        mapping = ((cfg.get("defaults") or {}).get("status_map") or {})
        return ({str(v): STATUS_ROLE[k] for k, v in mapping.items()
                 if k in STATUS_ROLE and v}, str(c), None)
    return {}, None, None


def read_board(path):
    """(cards, missing, error) from the file that atlassian-expert produced.

    Accepted formats: a list of `{"key": ..., "status": ...}`, or an object
    with `cards` (the same list) and `missing` (the keys Jira said do not
    exist). `missing` is explicit on purpose: a key that simply was not queried
    cannot be read as a deleted card — the difference between the two is
    `dropped` in someone's queue.
    """
    try:
        text = sys.stdin.read() if path == "-" else Path(path).read_text(encoding="utf-8")
        data = yaml.safe_load(text)
    except (yaml.YAMLError, OSError) as e:
        return None, None, f"{path} está ilegível ({e.__class__.__name__}: {e})"
    if isinstance(data, list):
        cards, missing_keys = data, []
    elif isinstance(data, dict):
        cards, missing_keys = (data.get("cards") or []), (data.get("missing") or [])
    else:
        return None, None, (f"{path} não tem nem uma lista de cards nem um "
                            "objeto com `cards` — não dá para reconciliar contra nada")
    output = {}
    for c in cards:
        if isinstance(c, dict) and c.get("key"):
            output[str(c["key"])] = str(c.get("status") or "")
    return output, [str(a) for a in missing_keys], None


def reconcile(items, board, missing_keys, role_of):
    """(divergences, in_sync, missing, warnings) — the plan × board table.

    Never closes `human_pending` (only the human closes it), never appends a
    card the plan does not have (a position without `why` is the decision the
    queue exists to keep), never invents a role for a status the map does not
    know and never demotes a `done` item (R3).
    """
    div, in_sync, warnings = [], [], []
    seen = set()
    for it in items:
        if not isinstance(it, dict):
            continue
        ident, st = str(it.get("id")), status_of(it)
        seen.add(ident)
        if st == "done" and (ident in missing_keys or ident in board):
            # R3 (owner, 2026-09-25): status goes from the board to the plan and
            # NEVER demotes a `done` item. Demoting on bounce reopened 11 finished
            # cards in wego-acesso-backend. The divergent board becomes a named
            # warning; reopening the item is the owner's decision, via /common:queue.
            raw = "(não existe mais)" if ident in missing_keys else board[ident]
            role = "descartado" if ident in missing_keys else role_of.get(raw)
            if role in ("done", "em-revisao"):
                in_sync.append(ident)
            else:
                warnings.append(
                    f"{ident} está `done` aqui e '{raw}' no quadro — não "
                    "rebaixei (regra R3: status nunca rebaixa item `done`). Se "
                    "o card reabriu de verdade, quem devolve o item à fila é o "
                    "dono, pelo /common:queue")
            continue
        if ident in missing_keys:
            if st == "dropped":
                # 2026-09-28-0558: an item already `dropped` in the queue and gone
                # from the board is not a divergence — listing `dropped → dropped`
                # is noise that hid the round's only real divergence.
                in_sync.append(ident)
            else:
                div.append({"id": ident, "de": st, "para": "dropped",
                            "board": "(não existe mais)", "leitura":
                            f"{ident} não existe mais no quadro — some da fila como "
                            "`dropped`, com o motivo, em vez de sumir calado"})
            continue
        if ident not in board:
            continue
        raw = board[ident]
        role = role_of.get(raw)
        if role is None:
            warnings.append(
                f"{ident} está em '{raw}', um status que o `status_map` do "
                "board-flow.yaml não descreve — não reconciliei este item, "
                "porque adivinhar o papel dele é inventar o estado do trabalho")
            continue
        if role == "descartado":
            if st == "dropped":
                # 2026-09-28-0558: same reason as the `missing_keys` branch above —
                # an item already `dropped` in the queue and discarded on the board
                # is not a divergence, it is noise.
                in_sync.append(ident)
            else:
                div.append({"id": ident, "de": st, "para": "dropped", "board": raw,
                            "leitura": f"o quadro descartou {ident} ({raw})"})
        elif role == "done" and st != "done":
            div.append({"id": ident, "de": st, "para": "done", "board": raw,
                        "leitura": f"{ident} fechou fora deste plano ({raw}). "
                        "A rota de validação humana dele NÃO veio junto: se "
                        "havia uma, ela está perdida — só você sabe dizer"})
        elif role in ("em-andamento", "em-revisao") and st == "pending":
            warnings.append(
                f"{ident} está '{raw}' no quadro e `pending` aqui — uma "
                "sessão pode estar nele agora; conferir antes de começá-lo")
            in_sync.append(ident)
        else:
            in_sync.append(ident)
    missing = sorted(k for k in board if k not in seen)
    return div, in_sync, missing, warnings


# ── landed: proven cards whose code already reached the integration branch ──
#
# On the overnight branch the rule is "no merge, no push, no Done": the card
# is proven there and stays in Review, which is right while the code lives
# only on that branch. `cepa-until land` then merges it into main and
# never speaks to Jira, so nothing moved those cards afterwards. On
# 2026-11-03 eleven WEGO cards sat in Review with PROVEN proof, complete
# acceptance and code on main since the landing (fb-20261103-1). This lists
# them; step 0 of /common:drain-plan sends them to Done through
# atlassian-expert, the same auto-advance `/board-flow:prove` applies when
# `defaults.status_map.done` is set.

LANDED_PROOF_DIRS = (("docs", "proof"), (".claude", "proof"))
LANDED_ACCEPTANCE_DIRS = ((".claude", "acceptance"), ("docs", "acceptance"))


def _first_yaml(root, dirs, key):
    for parts in dirs:
        p = Path(root).joinpath(*parts, f"{key}.yaml")
        if p.is_file():
            try:
                return p, (yaml.safe_load(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8")) or {})
            except (yaml.YAMLError, OSError):
                return p, None
    return None, None


def integration_ref(root, into=None):
    for ref in ([into] if into else ["origin/HEAD", "origin/main", "main"]):
        rc, out, _ = _git(root, "rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", ref)
        if rc == 0 and out.strip():
            return ref
    return None


def landed_check(root, key, ref):
    """(ready, reason): ready only with PROVEN proof, complete acceptance,
    validation when the topology asks for it, and the proof's head_commit
    contained in `ref`."""
    p, proof = _first_yaml(root, LANDED_PROOF_DIRS, key)
    if p is None:
        return False, "sem artefato de prova"
    if not isinstance(proof, dict):
        return False, f"{p} ilegível"
    verdict = str(proof.get("verdict") or "").lower().replace("_", "-")
    if verdict != "proven":
        return False, f"prova `{verdict or '<ausente>'}`, não proven"
    a, acc = _first_yaml(root, LANDED_ACCEPTANCE_DIRS, key)
    if a is None:
        return False, "sem auditoria de aceite"
    if not isinstance(acc, dict):
        return False, f"{a} ilegível (YAML inválido)"
    if str(acc.get("status") or "").lower() != "complete":
        return False, f"auditoria `{acc.get('status')}`, não complete"
    gap = missing_validation(root, key)
    if gap is not None:
        return False, "sem veredito do validation-lead"
    head = str(proof.get("head_commit") or "").strip()
    if not head:
        return False, "a prova não registra head_commit"
    rc, _, _ = _git(root, "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", head, ref)
    if rc != 0:
        return False, f"head_commit {head} ainda não está em {ref}"
    return True, f"proven, aceite completo, {head} em {ref}"


def cmd_landed(root, filename, config, into, as_json):
    board, _, error = read_board(filename)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    role_of, _, error = repo_status_map(root, config)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    review = [k for k, st in board.items() if role_of.get(st) == "em-revisao"]
    ref = integration_ref(root, into)
    if ref is None:
        print("não achei a branch de integração (origin/HEAD, origin/main, "
              "main); passe --into", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    ready, held = [], []
    for key in sorted(review):
        ok, why = landed_check(root, key, ref)
        (ready if ok else held).append({"key": key, "motivo": why})
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"into": ref, "prontos": ready, "retidos": held},
                         ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
        return 0
    print(f"{len(review)} card(s) em revisão; {len(ready)} pronto(s) para "
          f"Done (código em {ref}):")
    for r in ready:
        print(f"  {r['key']}: {r['motivo']}")
    for h in held:
        print(f"  · {h['key']} fica: {h['motivo']}")
    return 0


def cmd_reconcile(root, name, filename, config, apply_changes, as_json):
    target = queue_path(root, name)
    if not target.is_file():
        print(f"{target} não existe — não há fila para reconciliar. Quem escreve "
              "é o /common:queue.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    plan, error = read_plan(target)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if mode_of(plan) != MODE:
        print(f"{target} é um plano '{mode_of(plan)}', não uma fila — ondas se "
              "reconciliam pelo /maestro:resume", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    board, missing_keys, error = read_board(filename)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    role_of, cfg, error = repo_status_map(root, config)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if not role_of:
        print("nenhum `defaults.status_map` encontrado (board-flow.yaml ou "
              ".claude/board-flow.lifecycle.yaml) — sem ele os nomes de status "
              "deste time são desconhecidos, e mapear 'Doing' para um papel no "
              "chute é inventar o estado do trabalho", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    items = plan.get("items") or []
    div, in_sync, missing, warnings = reconcile(items, board, missing_keys, role_of)

    applied = []
    if apply_changes and div:
        by_id = {str(i.get("id")): i for i in items if isinstance(i, dict)}
        for d in div:
            it = by_id.get(d["id"])
            if it is None:
                continue
            it["status"] = d["para"]
            it["reconciled"] = {"at": now_iso(), "board": d["board"],
                                "de": d["de"], "para": d["para"]}
            applied.append(d["id"])
        write_body(target, plan, items)

    output = {"program": qp.queue_name_of(plan), "queue": qp.queue_name_of(plan),
             "path": str(target), "config": cfg,
             "divergences": div, "in_sync": in_sync, "missing_from_plan": missing,
             "warnings": warnings, "applied": applied, "wrote": bool(applied)}
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(output, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
        return 0

    print(f"fila {output['queue']} · {target} × quadro ({cfg})")
    if not div:
        print("  nenhuma divergência — o plano descreve o que o quadro mostra")
    for d in div:
        print(f"  {d['id']}: {d['de']} → {d['para']} · {d['leitura']}")
    if missing:
        print("  no quadro e FORA da fila (não anexados — posição sem `why` é "
              "a decisão que a fila guarda): " + ", ".join(missing))
        print("  quem os coloca é o /common:queue <nome> --from-jira")
    for a in warnings:
        print(f"  aviso: {a}")
    print(f"  {len(applied)} gravada(s)" if apply_changes else
          "  nada gravado (rode com --apply para gravar)")
    return 0


# ── order: the queue order applied to a list of Jira keys ────────────────────
#
# A2: until now /board-flow:drain ordered by Jira rank and
# /common:drain-plan / /common:next by the queue — raising a card's priority
# in Jira changed nothing in the plan. This subcommand gives drain the SAME
# order the queue already uses, without drain having to read the YAML itself.

def cmd_order(root, name, keys, as_json):
    target = queue_path(root, name)
    if not target.is_file():
        print(f"{target} não existe — sem fila para ordenar por ela; quem chama "
              "cai de volta para a ordem do Jira", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    plan, error = read_plan(target)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if mode_of(plan) != MODE:
        print(f"{target} é um plano '{mode_of(plan)}', não uma fila", file=sys.stderr)
        return 3

    items = plan.get("items") or []
    position = {str(it.get("id")): (i + 1, status_of(it))
               for i, it in enumerate(items) if isinstance(it, dict)}

    in_queue = sorted((k for k in keys if k in position), key=lambda k: position[k][0])
    excluded = [k for k in keys if k not in position]

    order = [{"key": k, "posicao": position[k][0], "status": position[k][1]}
             for k in in_queue]
    order += [{"key": k, "posicao": None, "status": None} for k in excluded]

    output = {"program": name, "queue": name, "ordem": order, "fora_do_plano": excluded}
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(output, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
        return 0

    print(f"fila {name} aplicada a {len(keys)} chave(s)")
    for o in order:
        mark = "" if o["posicao"] is not None else "  (fora do plano)"
        print(f"  {o['key']}{mark}")
    if excluded:
        print(f"  {len(excluded)} chave(s) fora do plano, na ordem do Jira: "
              + ", ".join(excluded))
    return 0


# ── divergence: the queue × the board × the BACKLOG, fixing nothing ─────────
#
# A3: what /common:doctor lists. Read-only on purpose — deciding here
# (closing an orphan card, inventing a `**Plano:**`) would be rewriting the queue
# or the BACKLOG without the owner seeing; whoever fixes is `add`,
# `reconcile --apply` or the owner's hand, after reading this report.

PLAN_MARK = "**Plano:**"
ID_IN_BACKTICKS = re.compile(r"`([^`]+)`")


def _backlog_sections(text):
    """[(heading, 1-based line, body)] — each `## ` level section."""
    lines = text.splitlines()
    marks = [(i, l[3:].strip()) for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith("## ")]
    sections = []
    for idx, (i, heading) in enumerate(marks):
        end = marks[idx + 1][0] if idx + 1 < len(marks) else len(lines)
        sections.append((heading, i + 1, lines[i + 1:end]))
    return sections


def _extract_plan(line):
    """The text after `**Plano:**` up to the next field, or None.

    The mark does not live alone on the line: in the real BACKLOG.md format it
    appears in the MIDDLE of a line of fields separated by ` · `, for example
    `**Status:** 🔵 ABERTO · **Plano:** \\`id\\` · **Lar:** ...`. Anchoring the
    search at the start of the line (as the previous version did) read that
    section as "without `**Plano:**`" — a false positive measured on the real
    BACKLOG. Here the mark is searched at ANY position, and the value runs to
    the next ` · ` (this convention's field separator) or the end of the line.
    """
    idx = line.find(PLAN_MARK)
    if idx == -1:
        return None
    rest = line[idx + len(PLAN_MARK):]
    cut_at = rest.find("·")
    if cut_at != -1:
        rest = rest[:cut_at]
    return rest.strip()


def backlog_divergence(text, name, queue_ids):
    """(sections_without_plan, nonexistent_plan) from the BACKLOG.md text.

    `**Plano:** <id1>, <id2>` may cite more than one plan (e.g. the Maestro
    section). An id with `/` is `<program>/<id-in-queue>` — it is only evaluated
    against THIS queue (`name`) when the program matches; an id without `/` is
    read as belonging to this queue. `**Plano:** fora da fila (motivo)` is
    exempt: it is the section explicitly saying there is no queue for it.

    The id is the text BETWEEN BACKTICKS, never the whole line after them: the
    real format appends loose text after the closed id, like
    `\\`cepa/baseline-cega-builds-longos\\` (descartado)`. Cutting only the
    backticks at the ends (as the previous version did) left the closing
    backtick glued to the id — it never matched anything in the queue, and a
    truly `dropped` item became a false positive of "nonexistent plan".
    """
    without_plan, nonexistent = [], []
    for heading, line, body in _backlog_sections(text):
        value = None
        for l in body:
            v = _extract_plan(l)
            if v is not None:
                value = v
                break
        if value is None:
            without_plan.append({"secao": heading, "linha": line})
            continue
        if value.startswith("fora da fila"):
            continue
        pieces = ID_IN_BACKTICKS.findall(value)
        if not pieces:
            # no backtick at all: fallback convention, a "bare" id per comma
            pieces = [p.strip() for p in value.split(",") if p.strip()]
        for piece in pieces:
            piece = piece.strip()
            if not piece:
                continue
            if "/" in piece:
                program, ident = piece.split("/", 1)
            else:
                program, ident = name, piece
            if program != name:
                continue
            if ident not in queue_ids:
                nonexistent.append({"secao": heading, "linha": line,
                                    "plano": piece})
    return without_plan, nonexistent


def cmd_divergence(root, name, board_file, backlog_file, as_json):
    target = queue_path(root, name)
    items, warnings = [], []
    if target.is_file():
        plan, error = read_plan(target)
        if error:
            print(error, file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        if mode_of(plan) != MODE:
            print(f"{target} é um plano '{mode_of(plan)}', não uma fila",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
        items = plan.get("items") or []
    else:
        warnings.append(f"{target} não existe — a fila '{name}' ainda não tem "
                      "plan.yaml; cards_sem_item e itens_com_card_done "
                      "comparam contra uma fila vazia")

    queue_ids = {str(it.get("id")) for it in items if isinstance(it, dict)}
    by_id = {str(it.get("id")): it for it in items if isinstance(it, dict)}

    cards_without_item, items_with_card_done = [], []
    if board_file:
        board, missing_keys, error = read_board(board_file)
        if error:
            print(error, file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        role_of, cfg, error = repo_status_map(root)
        if error:
            print(error, file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        if not role_of:
            warnings.append("nenhum `defaults.status_map` encontrado — não dá "
                          "para dizer se um card do quadro está aberto ou "
                          "fechado, então cards_sem_item e "
                          "itens_com_card_done ficaram de fora")
        else:
            for key, raw in board.items():
                role = role_of.get(raw)
                if role is None:
                    warnings.append(f"{key} está em '{raw}', que o "
                                  "`status_map` do board-flow.yaml não "
                                  "descreve — não avaliado, para não "
                                  "adivinhar o estado do trabalho")
                    continue
                if key not in queue_ids and role != "done":
                    cards_without_item.append({"key": key, "status": raw})
            for ident, it in by_id.items():
                if status_of(it) in ("done", "dropped"):
                    continue
                raw = board.get(ident)
                if raw is None:
                    continue
                if role_of.get(raw) == "done":
                    items_with_card_done.append(
                        {"id": ident, "status": status_of(it), "board": raw})
    else:
        warnings.append("sem `--board`: cards_sem_item e itens_com_card_done "
                      "não avaliados")

    sections_without_plan, nonexistent_plan = [], []
    if backlog_file:
        p = Path(backlog_file)
        if not p.is_file():
            print(f"{p} não existe", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        text = p.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
        sections_without_plan, nonexistent_plan = backlog_divergence(
            text, name, queue_ids)
    else:
        warnings.append("sem `--backlog`: secoes_sem_plano e "
                      "plano_inexistente não avaliados")

    output = {"program": name, "queue": name, "cards_sem_item": cards_without_item,
             "itens_com_card_done": items_with_card_done,
             "secoes_sem_plano": sections_without_plan,
             "plano_inexistente": nonexistent_plan, "avisos": warnings}
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(output, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
        return 0

    print(f"divergência da fila {name}")
    if cards_without_item:
        print("  cards abertos no quadro sem item no plano: " + ", ".join(
            f"{c['key']} ({c['status']})" for c in cards_without_item))
    if items_with_card_done:
        print("  itens não fechados cujo card o quadro já dá como done: "
              + ", ".join(f"{i['id']} ({i['status']})"
                          for i in items_with_card_done))
    if sections_without_plan:
        print("  seções do BACKLOG sem `**Plano:**`: " + ", ".join(
            f"{s['secao']} (linha {s['linha']})" for s in sections_without_plan))
    if nonexistent_plan:
        print("  `**Plano:**` citando id fora desta fila: " + ", ".join(
            f"{p['secao']} → {p['plano']}" for p in nonexistent_plan))
    for a in warnings:
        print(f"  aviso: {a}")
    return 0


def cmd_check_name(root, name):
    target = queue_path(root, name)
    if not target.is_file():
        print(f"nome livre: {target} não existe")
        return 0
    plan, error = read_plan(target)
    if error:
        print(f"{error} — não dá para dizer o que a fila sobrescreveria",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    mode = mode_of(plan)
    if mode == MODE:
        items = plan.get("items") or []
        print(f"nome ocupado por uma fila single-track ({len(items)} itens) — "
              f"reescrever é o fluxo normal de repriorizar '{name}'; o que veio "
              f"da execução (status, human_pending) é preservado")
        return 0
    print(f"COLISÃO: {target} é um plano '{mode}' — as ondas do "
          f"/maestro:program-plan. Gravar a fila aqui apaga as ondas e o "
          f"aceite de cada slice. Escolha outro nome de programa.",
          file=sys.stderr)
    return 3


def cmd_validate(arg, repo="."):
    p = Path(arg)
    if not p.is_file():
        # Not a file: it is a queue name, resolved at the main clone like every
        # other subcommand (a linked worktree's copy may be absent or stale).
        root = main_root(repo)
        if root is None:
            print(f"{arg} não é um arquivo, e {repo} não é um repositório git — "
                  "a fila mora no clone principal, e sem git não dá para "
                  "achá-lo", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        p = queue_path(root, arg)
        if not p.is_file():
            print(f"{arg} não existe como arquivo, e a fila '{arg}' não existe "
                  f"no clone principal ({p})", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    plan, error = read_plan(p)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    gaps = validate_plan(plan)
    if gaps:
        print(f"{p}: {len(gaps)} lacuna(s)", file=sys.stderr)
        for f in gaps:
            print(f"  - {f}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    print(f"{p}: fila válida, {len(plan.get('items') or [])} itens")
    return 0


def cmd_decisions(repo, files, as_json):
    """Lists, per file, the decisions of "Decided without asking" with and
    without a verdict. The reader is the one the readiness hook uses
    (`_decisions`), so the count here is the count the gate sees. Reads files
    only: no git needed."""
    base = Path(repo)
    if files:
        paths = [Path(f) for f in files]
        missing = [str(p) for p in paths if not p.is_file()]
        if missing:
            for m in missing:
                print(f"{m} não existe como arquivo", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        shown = [(p, str(p)) for p in paths]
    else:
        found = []
        for sub in ("spec", "epics"):
            d = base / "docs" / sub
            if d.is_dir():
                found += sorted(d.glob("*.md"))
        shown = [(p, str(p.relative_to(base))) for p in found]

    reports = []
    for path, label in shown:
        res = _decisions.read_file(path)
        if res is None:
            reports.append({"path": label, "decisions": None})
            continue
        every = sorted(res.pending + res.decided, key=lambda d: d.line)
        reports.append({"path": label, "decisions": [
            {"ordinal": i, "line": d.line, "text": d.text, "verdict": d.verdict}
            for i, d in enumerate(every, 1)]})

    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"files": reports}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))
        return 0
    if not reports:
        print("Nenhuma spec em docs/spec/ nem Epic em docs/epics/.")
        return 0
    for r in reports:
        decs = r["decisions"]
        if decs is None:
            print(f"{r['path']}: sem a seção \"Decided without asking\"")
            continue
        pending = [d for d in decs if not d["verdict"]]
        print(f"{r['path']}: {len(decs)} decisões, {len(pending)} sem veredito, "
              f"{len(decs) - len(pending)} com veredito")
        for d in pending:
            print(f"  #{d['ordinal']} (linha {d['line']}): {d['text']}")
    return 0


def _cites(source, rel):
    """True when the queue's free-text `source:` names `rel` as a whole path:
    `docs/spec/a.md (3 critérios)` and `./docs/spec/a.md` cite docs/spec/a.md;
    `docs/spec/xa.md`, `../docs/spec/a.md` and `docs/spec/a.md.bak` do not."""
    text = source if isinstance(source, str) else json.dumps(source, ensure_ascii=False)
    pat = r"(?<![\w./-])(?:\./)?" + re.escape(rel) + r"(?![\w/-]|\.\w)"
    return re.search(pat, text) is not None


def derived_queues(repo, rel):
    """[(queue, done, total)] of the single-track queues whose `source:` cites
    `rel`. The queues live in the main clone, as everywhere in this script."""
    root = main_root(repo) or Path(repo)
    out = []
    for name, qfile in qp.queue_files(root):
        plan, error = read_plan(qfile)
        if error or not isinstance(plan, dict) or mode_of(plan) != MODE:
            continue
        if not _cites(plan.get("source") or "", rel):
            continue
        items = [it for it in plan.get("items") or [] if isinstance(it, dict)]
        done = sum(1 for it in items if status_of(it) == "done")
        out.append((qp.queue_name_of(plan, name) or name, done, len(items)))
    return out


def _rel_to_repo(path, repo):
    """`path` as the queues cite it: relative to the repo root."""
    full = path.resolve()
    for base in (Path(repo).resolve(), ):
        try:
            return full.relative_to(base).as_posix()
        except ValueError:
            pass
    r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(full.parent), "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"],
                       capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode == 0:
        try:
            return full.relative_to(Path(r.stdout.strip()).resolve()).as_posix()
        except ValueError:
            pass
    return path.as_posix()


def cmd_verdict(repo, file, ordinal, verdict, reason, text, today=None):
    """Writes the owner's verdict on decision `ordinal` of the "Decided
    without asking" section of `file`, numbered as `cepa-plan decisions`
    numbers it. The marker is the one `_decisions` reads: `· mantida em
    <date>`, `· vetada em <date>: <reason>`, `· refinada em <date>`. Only that
    item changes; `Status` and every other line stay byte for byte.

    The veto is a record (O2'): it undoes nothing. What it does do, on vetada
    or refinada, is say when a queue was already derived from the file, so the
    owner knows code may already stand on the decision just changed.

    Exit 0 written; 1 refused (no section, ordinal out of range, item already
    has a verdict); 2 invalid usage (missing file, --reason or --text)."""
    path = Path(file)
    if verdict == "vetada" and not (reason or "").strip():
        print("vetada exige --reason: o motivo do veto é o que fica registrado "
              "na linha.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if verdict == "refinada":
        text = " ".join((text or "").split())
        if not text:
            print("refinada exige --text com o novo texto da decisão.",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        if _decisions.VERDICT_RE.search(text):
            print("--text já traz um marcador de veredito; passe só o texto da "
                  "decisão.", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    if not path.is_file():
        print(f"{file} não existe como arquivo", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    # newline="" on both ends: a CRLF file stays CRLF, byte for byte.
    with open(path, encoding="utf-8", newline="") as fh:
        raw = fh.read()
    res = _decisions.read(raw)
    if res is None:
        print(f"{file}: sem a seção \"Decided without asking\"", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    every = sorted(res.pending + res.decided, key=lambda d: d.line)
    if not 1 <= ordinal <= len(every):
        print(f"{file}: não há decisão #{ordinal}; a seção tem {len(every)} "
              f"(veja `cepa plan decisions {file}`)", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    d = every[ordinal - 1]
    if d.verdict:
        print(f"{file}: a decisão #{ordinal} (linha {d.line}) já tem veredito "
              f"({d.verdict}); um veredito não se reescreve.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    day = today or datetime.now().date().isoformat()
    marker = f" · {verdict} em {day}"
    if (reason or "").strip():
        marker += ": " + " ".join(reason.split())

    lines = raw.splitlines(keepends=True)
    first, last = d.line - 1, (d.end or d.line) - 1

    def ending(line):
        return line[len(line.rstrip("\r\n")):]

    if verdict == "refinada":
        head = lines[first]
        bullet = re.match(r"^([-*+]\s+)", head).group(1)
        new = [bullet + text + marker + ending(lines[last])]
        lines[first:last + 1] = new
        shown = new[0].rstrip("\r\n")
    else:
        body = lines[last].rstrip("\r\n")
        lines[last] = body.rstrip() + marker + ending(lines[last])
        shown = lines[last].rstrip("\r\n")

    tmp = path.with_name(path.name + ".verdict-tmp")
    with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="") as fh:
        fh.write("".join(lines))
    os.replace(tmp, path)

    print(f"{file}: decisão #{ordinal} (linha {d.line}) {verdict}.")
    print(f"  {shown.strip()}")
    if verdict in ("vetada", "refinada"):
        for q, done, total in derived_queues(repo, _rel_to_repo(path, repo)):
            if done:
                word = "item done" if done == 1 else "itens done"
                print(f"Atenção: isto já virou código na fila {q}: {done} {word} "
                      f"de {total}. O veto é registro e não desfaz nada; se o "
                      f"código precisar mudar, isso é item novo na fila.")
            else:
                print(f"Atenção: a fila {q} foi derivada deste arquivo "
                      f"(0 itens done de {total}); revise os itens pendentes "
                      f"antes de rodá-la.")
    return 0


def cmd_write(root, a):
    if a.from_triage:
        handoff, error = read_handoff(a.from_triage)
        if error:
            print(error, file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        items, warnings, errors = items_from_triage(handoff)
        for warning in warnings:
            print(f"aviso: {warning}", file=sys.stderr)
        if errors:
            for e in errors:
                print(f"recusa: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        error = None
    elif a.from_spec:
        sp = Path(a.from_spec)
        if not sp.is_file():
            print(f"{sp} não existe", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        items, warnings = items_from_spec(sp.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        for warning in warnings:
            print(f"aviso: {warning}", file=sys.stderr)
        if not items:
            print(f"{sp} não tem nenhum critério de sucesso (`### CS-N: ...`)",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        error = None
    elif a.from_epic:
        read_result = read_epic(a.from_epic, a.cycle)
        if read_result is None:
            return 2
        epic_demonstrates, items, epic_source = read_result
        error = None
    else:
        items, error = load_items(a.items)
    if error:
        print(error, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    gaps = validate_items(items)
    if gaps:
        print(f"{len(gaps)} lacuna(s) na fila — nada foi gravado",
              file=sys.stderr)
        for f in gaps:
            print(f"  - {f}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    target = queue_path(root, a.name)
    old_items, old_source, old_demonstrates, old_key = [], None, None, None
    if target.is_file():
        plan, err = read_plan(target)
        if err:
            print(f"{err} — não dá para dizer o que seria sobrescrito",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
        if mode_of(plan) != MODE:
            print(f"COLISÃO: {target} é um plano '{mode_of(plan)}' — as ondas do "
                  f"/maestro:program-plan. Gravar a fila aqui apaga as ondas e "
                  f"o aceite de cada slice. Escolha outro nome de programa.",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
        old_items = plan.get("items") or []
        # the legacy queue keeps the key it has until it migrates
        old_key = "queue" if "queue" in plan else "program"
        old_source = plan.get("source")
        # Reprioritizing touches the items, not what the queue demonstrates: the field
        # comes from disk, otherwise the first rewrite erases it silently.
        old_demonstrates = _read_demonstrates(plan)

        new_ids = {str(i.get("id")) for i in items}
        vanished = [str(x.get("id")) for x in old_items
                   if isinstance(x, dict) and str(x.get("id")) not in new_ids]
        # With --from-triage there is no refusal: `done`/`dropped` outside the list are
        # preserved silently (they are not executable, their position does not
        # move the queue) and the absent open ones go after the triage order.
        if vanished and a.on_missing == "refuse" and not a.from_triage:
            print(f"a fila que está no disco tem {len(vanished)} item(ns) que a "
                  f"lista nova não menciona: {', '.join(vanished)}.\n"
                  "Sumir com eles em silêncio apaga posição e `why` que alguém "
                  "decidiu. Inclua-os na lista, ou diga explicitamente o que "
                  "fazer: --on-missing keep (mantém no fim, sem posição "
                  "escolhida) ou --on-missing drop (marca status: dropped). "
                  "Só --from-triage dispensa a escolha: `done`/`dropped` "
                  "ausentes são preservados, e os abertos ausentes vão para "
                  "depois da ordem da triagem.",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 4

    merged, reused = merge(items, old_items)
    appended, pushed_back = [], []
    if old_items:
        new_ids = {str(i["id"]) for i in merged}
        leftovers = [x for x in old_items
                  if isinstance(x, dict) and str(x.get("id")) not in new_ids]
        no_why = "sem `why` registrado na fila anterior"
        if a.from_triage and a.on_missing != "keep" and leftovers:
            # Order approved in the triage (fb-20261002-1): the absent closed ones
            # stay as a block, in the old order, before everything (they are not
            # executable, so position does not move the queue); the triage's
            # items come in its order; the open ones it did not cite go
            # after, in the old order (refuse) or become `dropped` (drop).
            closed = [normalize({**s, "why": s.get("why") or no_why})
                        for s in leftovers if s.get("status") in CLOSED]
            open_items = [s for s in leftovers if s.get("status") not in CLOSED]
            after_items = []
            for s in open_items:
                d = normalize({**s, "why": s.get("why") or no_why})
                if a.on_missing == "drop":
                    d["status"] = "dropped"
                else:
                    pushed_back.append(str(s.get("id")))
                after_items.append(d)
            merged = closed + merged + after_items
        elif a.on_missing == "keep" and a.from_triage and leftovers:
            # PARTIAL triage: the handoff covers a piece of the column, so the
            # order it proposes holds among the cards it read, not against the
            # queue the owner already prioritized. Found on a real board
            # (2026-09-25): 3 new cards entered ahead of the 5 prioritized
            # pending ones, and those went to the end. The disk queue stays in
            # its position (an item the triage also cites is updated right
            # there) and the new cards enter AFTER, in the triage order.
            by_id = {str(f["id"]): f for f in merged}
            already_in_queue = []
            for s in old_items:
                if not isinstance(s, dict):
                    continue
                ident = str(s.get("id"))
                already_in_queue.append(by_id.pop(ident) if ident in by_id else
                                  normalize({**s, "why": s.get("why") or
                                             "sem `why` registrado na fila anterior"}))
            appended = [str(f["id"]) for f in merged
                             if str(f["id"]) in by_id]
            merged = already_in_queue + [f for f in merged
                                     if str(f["id"]) in by_id]
        elif a.on_missing == "keep":
            merged.extend(normalize({**s, "why": s.get("why") or
                                       "sem `why` registrado na fila anterior"}
                                      ) for s in leftovers)
        elif a.on_missing == "drop":
            for s in leftovers:
                d = normalize({**s, "why": s.get("why") or
                               "sem `why` registrado na fila anterior"})
                d["status"] = "dropped"
                merged.append(d)

    if pushed_back:
        print(f"aviso: {len(pushed_back)} item(ns) aberto(s) da fila do disco "
              f"não estão na triagem e ficaram depois da ordem dela: "
              f"{', '.join(pushed_back)}", file=sys.stderr)

    source = a.source or (
        f"{a.from_spec} ({len(items)} critérios de sucesso; ordem herdada do texto)"
        if a.from_spec else None) or (
        triage_source(handoff) if a.from_triage else None
        ) or (epic_source if a.from_epic else None
        ) or old_source or "ditada à mão em /common:queue"
    # With --from-epic the `demonstrates:` is the cycle's script and comes from the Epic, which is
    # where it is decided; in the other sources it comes from disk, untouched.
    text = serialize(a.name, source, merged, a.when or "(data não informada)",
                      epic_demonstrates if a.from_epic else old_demonstrates,
                      key=old_key or "queue")

    if a.dry_run:
        print(text)
        return 0

    backup = None
    target.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    if target.is_file():
        backup = target.with_name(target.name + ".bak")
        backup.write_text(target.read_text(encoding="utf-8"), encoding="utf-8")
    tmp = target.with_suffix(".yaml.tmp")
    tmp.write_text(text, encoding="utf-8")
    tmp.replace(target)

    print(f"gravado: {target}")
    print(f"  {len(merged)} itens · fonte: {source}")
    if reused:
        print(f"  {len(reused)} item(ns) já existiam — status e "
              f"human_pending preservados do disco: {', '.join(reused)}")
    if appended:
        print(f"  triagem parcial: a ordem da fila do disco foi mantida; "
              f"{len(appended)} card(s) novo(s) entraram depois dela: "
              f"{', '.join(appended)}")
    if pushed_back:
        print(f"  ordem da triagem aplicada: {len(pushed_back)} item(ns) "
              f"aberto(s) fora da triagem ficaram DEPOIS dela, na ordem "
              f"antiga: {', '.join(pushed_back)}")
    if backup:
        print(f"  cópia do anterior em {backup} — comentários escritos à mão "
              f"não sobrevivem à reescrita, estão lá")
    return 0


# ── migrate: .claude/programs/<n>/plan.yaml → .claude/queues/<n>/queue.yaml ─
#
# Owner's decision (2026-10-20): the single-track queue is now called `queue`,
# as in docs/how-it-fits.md. During the transition every consumer reads both
# layouts (`_queuepath`); this subcommand moves the existing queues. The maestro
# waves plan is NOT a queue and stays where it is.

def _tracked(root, rel):
    rc, out, _ = _git(root, "ls-files", "--", rel)
    return rc == 0 and bool(out.strip())


def _rewrite_key(qfile):
    """`program:` → `queue:` on the top key, line by line (comments and
    the rest of the text stay as they are; no YAML dump)."""
    text = qfile.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    if re.search(r"^queue:", text, re.M):
        return False
    new, n = re.subn(r"^program:", "queue:", text, count=1, flags=re.M)
    if not n:
        # Queue without `program:` at the top: without this it would come out "migrated" with no name
        # written. The key goes in before the first line that is not a comment.
        lines = text.splitlines(keepends=True)
        i = next((k for k, l in enumerate(lines)
                  if l.strip() and not l.lstrip().startswith("#")), len(lines))
        lines.insert(i, f"queue: {qfile.parent.name}\n")
        new = "".join(lines)
    qfile.write_text(new, encoding="utf-8")
    return True


def _live_run(old_dir):
    """Is a `cepa-until` of this queue alive right now? Same rule as the
    `run_vivo_da_fila` / `supervisor_vivo` of cepa-until: `until/*.estado.json`
    with state `rodando`, pid alive on this machine and whose command is a
    `cepa-until`. Between two items there is no `in_progress`, and the live run
    holds `until/` open: moving the folder from under it splits the record in two."""
    import socket
    host = socket.gethostname()
    for path in sorted((old_dir / "until").glob("*.estado.json")):
        try:
            est = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        if not isinstance(est, dict) or est.get("estado") != "rodando":
            continue
        pid = est.get("pid")
        if not pid or (est.get("host") and est.get("host") != host):
            continue
        try:
            os.kill(int(pid), 0)
        except ProcessLookupError:
            continue
        except PermissionError:
            pass
        except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError):
            continue
        r = subprocess.run(["ps", "-o", "command=", "-p", str(int(pid))],
                           capture_output=True, text=True)
        if "cepa-until" in r.stdout:
            return f"run {est.get('run') or path.name}, pid {pid}"
    return None


def migrate_one(root, name, dry_run):
    """(state, message): state in migrada | nada | pulada | recusada."""
    old_dir = Path(root) / qp.LEGACY_DIR / name
    old = old_dir / qp.LEGACY_FILE
    new_dir = Path(root) / qp.NEW_DIR / name
    if not old.is_file():
        return "nada", f"{name}: nada a migrar (sem {old})"
    plan, error = read_plan(old)
    if error:
        return "recusada", f"{name}: {error} — nada foi movido"
    if mode_of(plan) != MODE:
        return "pulada", (f"{name}: é um plano '{mode_of(plan)}' (ondas do "
                          "maestro), não uma fila — fica em .claude/programs")
    if new_dir.exists():
        return "recusada", (f"{name}: o destino {new_dir} já existe — nada foi "
                            "movido; resolva à mão qual dos dois vale")
    for it in plan.get("items") or []:
        if isinstance(it, dict) and status_of(it) == "in_progress":
            state, detail = reservation_of(it, root)
            if state == "viva":
                return "recusada", (f"{name}: o item {it.get('id')} está "
                                    f"reservado por uma sessão VIVA ({detail}) "
                                    "— nada foi movido; migre depois que ela acabar")
    live_run = _live_run(old_dir)
    if live_run:
        return "recusada", (f"{name}: um cepa-until desta fila está rodando "
                            f"({live_run}) — nada foi movido; migre depois que o "
                            "run acabar")
    old_rel = _queue_rel(root, old_dir)
    new_rel = _queue_rel(root, new_dir)
    file_rel = _queue_rel(root, old)
    if _tracked(root, file_rel):
        _, dirty, _ = _git(root, "status", "--porcelain", "--", file_rel)
        if dirty.strip():
            return "recusada", (f"{name}: {file_rel} tem mudanças não "
                                "commitadas — commite a fila antes; o commit "
                                "da migração só move, não leva status de item")
    if dry_run:
        return "migrada", (f"{name}: moveria {old_rel}/ → {new_rel}/, "
                           f"{qp.LEGACY_FILE} → {qp.NEW_FILE}, `program:` → `queue:`")
    tracked = _tracked(root, old_rel)
    new_dir.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    if tracked:
        rc, _, err = _git(root, "mv", old_rel, new_rel)
        if rc != 0:
            return "recusada", f"{name}: git mv falhou ({err.strip()}) — nada foi movido"
    else:
        old_dir.rename(new_dir)
    for old_name, new_name in ((qp.LEGACY_FILE, qp.NEW_FILE),
                                  (qp.LEGACY_FILE + ".bak", qp.NEW_FILE + ".bak")):
        src, dst = new_dir / old_name, new_dir / new_name
        if not src.exists():
            continue
        try:
            if tracked and _tracked(root, _queue_rel(root, src)):
                rc, _, err = _git(root, "mv", _queue_rel(root, src),
                                  _queue_rel(root, dst))
                if rc != 0:
                    raise OSError(err.strip() or "git mv falhou")
            else:
                src.rename(dst)
        except OSError as e:
            return "recusada", (f"{name}: a pasta já foi para {new_rel}/, mas "
                                f"renomear {old_name} → {new_name} falhou "
                                f"({e}) — estado MEIO-MOVIDO, nada commitado; "
                                "termine à mão")
    _rewrite_key(new_dir / qp.NEW_FILE)
    msg = f"{name}: movida para {new_rel}/{qp.NEW_FILE}"
    if tracked:
        _git(root, "add", "-A", "--", old_rel, new_rel)
        message = f"queue {name}: .claude/programs → .claude/queues (cepa-plan migrate)"
        rc, _, err = _git(root, "commit", "-q", "-m", message, "--",
                          old_rel, new_rel)
        if rc == 0:
            _, sha, _ = _git(root, "rev-parse", "--short", "HEAD")
            msg += f" · commit {sha.strip()}"
        else:
            reason = [l for l in (err or "").strip().splitlines() if l.strip()]
            msg += (" · aviso: movida mas NÃO commitada "
                    f"({reason[-1] if reason else 'o git falhou'})")
    return "migrada", msg


def cmd_migrate(root, name, all_queues, dry_run):
    if bool(name) == bool(all_queues):
        print("migrate pede UM nome de fila ou --all", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if name:
        names = [name]
    else:
        names = [n for n, qfile in qp.queue_files(root)
                 if qfile.parent.parent.name == "programs"]
    moved, refused = 0, 0
    for n in names:
        state, msg = migrate_one(root, n, dry_run)
        if state == "pulada" and all_queues:
            print(f"pulada · {msg}")
        elif state == "pulada":
            print(f"recusa: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
            refused += 1
        elif state == "recusada":
            print(f"recusa: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
            refused += 1
        elif state == "migrada":
            print(("(dry-run) " if dry_run else "migrada · ") + msg)
            moved += 1
        else:
            if name and (Path(root) / qp.NEW_DIR / n / qp.NEW_FILE).is_file():
                print(f"{n}: já está em {qp.NEW_DIR}/{n}/{qp.NEW_FILE} — nada a migrar")
            elif name:
                print(f"{msg}", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
    if not moved and not refused:
        print("nada a migrar")
    return 3 if refused else 0


def main(argv=None):
    repo_help = "repository root (default: the current directory)"
    json_help = "JSON output, for code"
    commit_help = ("commits the queue (only it) in the same step; without it "
                   "the output says a commit is missing")
    not_git = "--repo is not a git repository"
    waves = "the name holds a waves plan (/maestro:program-plan), not a queue"
    no_queue = "the queue does not exist or cannot be read"

    ap = _clihelp.Parser(
        prog="cepa plan",
        description=(
            "The queue (.claude/queues/<name>/queue.yaml) is the document that keeps\n"
            "the ORDER of the items and the WHY of each position, which is what a\n"
            "tracker loses. This script is its mechanical writer: it validates,\n"
            "resolves the right root, refuses collisions and writes. /common:queue\n"
            "drives the conversation; /common:drain-plan and cepa until execute;\n"
            "/common:next and /common:queue-status read.\n"
            "\n"
            "It knows only `mode: single-track`. A wave plan is another document,\n"
            "with another author (/maestro:program-plan) and another reader\n"
            "(/maestro:run)."),
        groups=[
            ("sources (read only, return JSON)", ["from-spec", "from-epic", "from-triage"]),
            ("writing", ["write", "add", "verdict", "migrate", "check-name", "validate"]),
            ("reading", ["queue", "status", "show", "epics", "decisions", "promote", "order"]),
            ("one item's cycle", ["start", "finish", "answer"]),
            ("against the Jira board", ["reconcile", "landed", "divergence"]),
        ],
        examples=[
            ("cepa plan write wego --from-spec docs/spec/assinatura.md",
             "one item per success criterion"),
            ("cepa plan write wego --from-epic docs/epics/wego.md --cycle 2",
             "the queue of one Epic cycle"),
            ("cepa plan status", "the whole queue, by status"),
            ("cepa plan show wego WEGO-123", "one item in full, nothing cut"),
            ("cepa plan queue wego --max 3", "what the next batch may execute"),
            ("cepa plan start wego WEGO-123", "reserve an item"),
            ('cepa plan finish wego WEGO-123 --status done --evidence "commit abc, build green"',
             "record the outcome"),
        ],
        exit_codes=[
            (0, "the subcommand succeeded (each subcommand lists its own codes)"),
            (2, "invalid usage: no subcommand, unknown subcommand or option, "
                "--repo outside git"),
        ],
        see_also=["/common:queue: the conversation that calls `cepa plan write`",
                  "/common:next: names the next step from the queue",
                  "/common:drain-plan: runs the queue in batch"])
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd")

